@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/1308.0994/BoxdotConjecture.lean
@decl Arxiv.«1308.0994».NormalModalLogic
-- L4DEL: title: A “normal modal logic” L is any `Set Formula` such that: 1
-- L4DEL: intuition: A “normal modal logic” L is any `Set Formula` such that: 1. If `K ⊢ φ`, then `φ ∈ L` (L extends K) 2. If `φ ∈ L` and `(φ ~> ψ) ∈ L`, then `ψ ∈ L` (Closed under MP) 3. If `φ ∈ L`, then `□φ ∈ L` (Closed under Necessitation) 4. If `φ ∈ L`, then `φ.subst σ ∈ L` for every substitution `σ` (Closed under Uniform Substitution)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/1308.0994/BoxdotConjecture.lean
@decl Arxiv.«1308.0994».t
-- L4DEL: title: `t φ` is the Boxdot translation of a formula `φ`
-- L4DEL: intuition: `t φ` is the Boxdot translation of a formula `φ`. Roughly, t is the mapping `φ ↦ t φ` from the language of monomodal logic into itself that preserves variables and the logical constant `⊥`, commutes with the standard truth-functional operators, and is such that `t □a` = `□t a & t a`. This implementation follows the definition in Steinsvold (AJL).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

