@decl Arxiv.«2107.00295».independentDominationEven
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 1.6 (Even case).** For a nonempty isolate-free graph $G$ on $n$ vertices, if $D$ is even, then $(D + 2)^2 \cdot i(G) \leq (D^2 + 4) \cdot n$
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Conjecture 1.6 (Even case).** For a nonempty isolate-free graph $G$ on $n$ vertices, if $D$ is even, then $(D + 2)^2 \cdot i(G) \leq (D^2 + 4) \cdot n$. Proved by Cho, Kim, Kim and Oum (arxiv/2202.09594, Corollary 1.3).
