@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2602.05192/FirstProof6.lean
@decl Arxiv.«2602.05192».IsEpsilonLight
-- L4DEL: title: For a graph $G = (V, E)$, let $G_S = (V, E(S,S))$ denote the graph with the same vertex set, but only the edges between vertices in $S$
-- L4DEL: intuition: For a graph $G = (V, E)$, let $G_S = (V, E(S,S))$ denote the graph with the same vertex set, but only the edges between vertices in $S$. Let $L$ be the Laplacian matrix of $G$ and let $L_S$ be the Laplacian of $G_S$. I say that a set of vertices $S$ is $\epsilon$-light if the matrix $\epsilon L - L_S$ is positive semidefinite.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

