@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2605.02731/DeanCycles.lean
@decl Arxiv.«2605.02731».dean_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 1.1 (Dean, 1988).** For every integer $k \geq 3$, every finite simple graph with minimum degree at least $k$ contains a cycle whose length is divisible by $k$
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Conjecture 1.1 (Dean, 1988).** For every integer $k \geq 3$, every finite simple graph with minimum degree at least $k$ contains a cycle whose length is divisible by $k$. A cycle has length at least `3`, so the divisor is never `0` and the statement is not satisfied for a trivial reason. `SimpleGraph.minDegree` is `0` on a graph with no vertices and on a graph with no edges, so the hypothesis excludes both.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

