@decl Arxiv.«2607.05349».weighting
-- L4DEL: title: The weighting $\vec{w}(t) = Z(t)^{-1}\mathbf{1}$ at scale `t`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The weighting $\vec{w}(t) = Z(t)^{-1}\mathbf{1}$ at scale `t`. `Matrix.inv` is `0` on singular matrices, so this is only the intended vector where `Z t` is invertible. The analytic function `t ↦ det (Z t)` tends to `1` as `t → ∞`, so its zeros are isolated. Hence `Z t` is invertible for all small enough `t > 0`, as required below.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

