-- L4DEL: intuition: $x_n$ takes an integer value. Stated as $A_n \mid B_n$ rather than as `∃ m : ℤ, x n = m`, so that it still says the right thing if $A_n$ were ever $0$. There $x_n$ is a pole of the tangent rather than an integer, but `(B n : ℚ) / 0` is `0` in Lean and would count as one. The two agree whenever $A_n \neq 0$, which holds for every $n \leq 3000$.
