@decl Arxiv.«2607.08366».IsValidMod
-- L4DEL: title: `A` is *valid mod* `N` when the all-ones multiset is the only multiset of size `#A` drawn from `A` whose sum matches `∑ a ∈ A, a`
-- L4DEL: intuition: `A` is *valid mod* `N` when the all-ones multiset is the only multiset of size `#A` drawn from `A` whose sum matches `∑ a ∈ A, a`. `m a` is how many copies of `a` the multiset uses. The all-ones multiset has `m a = 1` for every `a ∈ A`; values outside `A` do not affect the sums.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

