@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/2607.08366/MinModulus.lean
@decl Arxiv.«2607.08366».min_modulus
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 1 (Fonollosa, 2026).** For every $n \geq 2$ and every $N < 2^n - 2^{\lfloor \log_2 n\rfloor}$, no set of $n$ residues mod $N$ is valid
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Conjecture 1 (Fonollosa, 2026).** For every $n \geq 2$ and every $N < 2^n - 2^{\lfloor \log_2 n\rfloor}$, no set of $n$ residues mod $N$ is valid. Equivalently the super-increasing set $\{2^k - 1 : 0 \leq k \leq n-1\}$ attains the least valid modulus, which is `minModulus n`. `0 < N` excludes `N = 0`, where `ZMod 0` is `ℤ` rather than a finite modulus and `{1, 2}` is valid, which would make the statement false for a reason unrelated to the question.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

