-- L4DEL: intuition: **Finite generation conjecture** (Etingof–Ostrik, Conjecture 2.18, algebra part). For every finite-dimensional Hopf algebra $A$ over a field $k$, the cohomology ring $H^*(A, k) = \mathrm{Ext}^*_A(k, k)$ is a finitely generated $k$-algebra.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/math.0301027/FiniteGenerationOfCohomology.lean
@decl HopfAlgebraCohomology.cohomologyRing_finiteType_monoidAlgebra
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: cohomologyRing_finiteType_monoidAlgebra
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Evens–Venkov.** For a finite group $G$ and a field $k$, the cohomology ring $H^*(G, k) = \mathrm{Ext}^*_{k[G]}(k, k)$ of the group algebra $k[G]$ is a finitely generated $k$-algebra.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Arxiv/math.0301027/FiniteGenerationOfCohomology.lean
@decl HopfAlgebraCohomology.cohomologyRing_finiteType_of_isCocomm
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: cohomologyRing_finiteType_of_isCocomm
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Friedlander–Suslin.** If $A$ is a finite-dimensional cocommutative Hopf algebra over a field $k$, that is, the group algebra of a finite group scheme over $k$, then $H^*(A, k)$ is a finitely generated $k$-algebra.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

