@decl Bugeaud06.isGenuinelySublacunary_of_isLacunary
-- L4DEL: title: A ratio floor is weaker than lacunarity: a lacunary sequence has ratios bounded below by a constant $> 1$, which dominates $1 + c/\log n$
-- L4DEL: intuition: A ratio floor is weaker than lacunarity: a lacunary sequence has ratios bounded below by a constant $> 1$, which dominates $1 + c/\log n$. So `IsGenuinelySublacunary` is a floor under the ratios, not a denial of lacunarity.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

