@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1036.lean
@decl Erdos1036.erdos_1036
-- L4DEL: title: Let $G$ be a graph on $n$ vertices which does not contain a trivial (empty or complete) graph on more than $c\log n$ vertices
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $G$ be a graph on $n$ vertices which does not contain a trivial (empty or complete) graph on more than $c\log n$ vertices. Must $G$ contain at least $2^{\Omega_c(n)}$ many induced subgraphs which are not pairwise isomorphic? This is true, and was proved by Shelah [Sh98].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

