@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1048.lean
@decl Erdos1048.erdos_1048
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_1048
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $f\in \mathbb{C}[x]$ is a monic polynomial with all roots satisfying $\lvert z\rvert \leq r$ for some $0 < r < 2$, then must $$\{ z: \lvert f(z)\rvert <1\}$$ have a connected component with diameter $>2-r$? A problem of Erdős, Herzog, and Piranian [EHP58]. Pommerenke [Po61] proved the answer is no for $r>1$, showing that if $f(z)=z^n-r^n$ then $\{ z: \lvert f(z)\rvert \leq 1\}$ has $n$ connected components, all with diameter $\to 0$ as $n\to \infty$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

