@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1063.lean
@decl Erdos1063.erdos_1063.better_upper
-- L4DEL: title: Estimate $n_k$ by finding a better upper bound than Cambie's $n_k \leq k \cdot \operatorname{lcm}(1, \dotsc, k-1)$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Estimate $n_k$ by finding a better upper bound than Cambie's $n_k \leq k \cdot \operatorname{lcm}(1, \dotsc, k-1)$. The comparator takes its least common multiple in `ℕ` and casts the result. Writing the ascription as `((… ).lcm (fun n : ℕ => n) : ℝ)` instead puts it on the `Finset.lcm` application, so the coercion lands on `n` and the `lcm` is taken in `ℝ`, where `lcm` of non-zero elements is `1` and the whole comparator collapses to `k`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

