-- L4DEL: title: Let $f_d(n)$ be the minimal $m$ such that any set of $m$ points in $\mathbb{R}^d$ contains a set of $n$ points for which any two determined distances are distinct
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $f_d(n)$ be the minimal $m$ such that any set of $m$ points in $\mathbb{R}^d$ contains a set of $n$ points for which any two determined distances are distinct. Erdős Problem 1088 asks to estimate $f_d(n)$. In particular, is it true that, for every fixed $n \geq 3$, $$ f_d(n) = 2^{o(d)} $$ as $d \to \infty$? The little-$o$ condition is stated after taking the base-$2$ logarithm.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

