@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1098.lean
@decl Erdos1098.erdos_1098
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_1098
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $G$ be a group and $\Gamma=\Gamma(G)$ be the non-commuting graph, with vertices the elements of $G$ and an edge between $g$ and $h$ if and only if $g$ and $h$ do not commute, $gh\neq hg$. If $\Gamma$ contains no infinite complete subgraph, then is there a finite bound on the size of complete subgraphs of $\Gamma$? This was solved by Neumann [Ne76], who proved that $\Gamma$ contains no infinite complete subgraph if and only if the centre of the group has finite index, and noted that if the centre has index $n$ then $\Gamma$ contains no complete subgraph on $>n$ vertices.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

