-- L4DEL: intuition: **Mertens' third theorem** [Me1874], in the weakened form the linked proof assumes: the product over the primes up to $n$ of $1 - 1/p$ is at least $1/(3\log n)$. The true asymptotic is $e^{-\gamma}/\log n$, and $e^{-\gamma} > 1/3$, so this bound is weaker than the theorem and is what the deduction needs.
