@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1146.lean
@decl Erdos1146.erdos_1146
-- L4DEL: title: Is $B=\{2^m3^n : m,n\geq 0\}$ an essential component?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is $B=\{2^m3^n : m,n\geq 0\}$ an essential component? In [Ru99] Ruzsa states "The simplest set with a chance to be an essential component is the collection of numbers in the form $2^m3^n$ and Erdős often asked whether it is an essential component or not; I do not even have a plausible guess."
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1146.lean
@decl Erdos1146.IsEssentialComponent
-- L4DEL: title: We say that $A\subset \mathbb{N}$ is an essential component if $d_s(A \oplus B)>d_s(B)$ for every $B\subset \mathbb{N}$ with $0<d_s(B)<1$ where $d_s$ is the Schnirelmann density
-- L4DEL: intuition: We say that $A\subset \mathbb{N}$ is an essential component if $d_s(A \oplus B)>d_s(B)$ for every $B\subset \mathbb{N}$ with $0<d_s(B)<1$ where $d_s$ is the Schnirelmann density. Here, the sumset is the appropriate one for Schnirelmann density, $A \oplus B = \{a+b \mid a \in A \cup \{0\}, b \in B \cup \{0\}\}$ (i.e. $(A \cup \{0\}) + (B \cup \{0\})$). This avoids the trivial case where the sumset misses $1$ simply because neither $A$ nor $B$ contains $0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/1147.lean
@decl Erdos1147.erdos_1147.variants.almost_every
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: almost_every
-- L4DEL: intuition: Konieczny [Ko16b] showed that, given any $\epsilon(n)\to 0$, the set $\{ n\geq 1: \| \alpha n^2\| < \epsilon(n)\}$ is not an additive basis of order $2$ for almost every $\alpha>0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

