@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/115.lean
@decl Erdos115.erdos_115
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_115
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $p(z)$ is a polynomial of degree $n$ such that $\{z : \lvert p(z)\rvert\leq 1\}$ is connected then is it true that $$\max_{\substack{z\in\mathbb{C}\\ \lvert p(z)\rvert\leq 1}} \lvert p'(z)\rvert \leq (\tfrac{1}{2}+o(1))n^2?$$ Eremenko and Lempert [ErLe94] have shown this is true, and in fact Chebyshev polynomials are the extreme examples.
