@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/119.lean
@decl Erdos119.erdos_119.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Is it true that $\limsup M_n = \infty$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is it true that $\limsup M_n = \infty$? This is Problem 4.1 in [Ha74] where it is attributed to Erdős. The weaker conjecture that $\limsup M_n=\infty$ was proved by Wagner [Wa80], who show that there is some $c>0$ with $M_n>(\log n)^c$ infinitely often.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/119.lean
@decl Erdos119.erdos_119.parts.ii
-- L4DEL: title: Is it true that there exists $c > 0$ such that for infinitely many $n$ we have $M_n > n^c$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is it true that there exists $c > 0$ such that for infinitely many $n$ we have $M_n > n^c$? The second question was answered by Beck [Be91], who proved that there exists some $c>0$ such that $\max_{n\leq N} M_n > N^c$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/119.lean
@decl Erdos119.erdos_119.parts.iii
-- L4DEL: title: Is it true that there exists $c > 0$ such that, for all large $n$, $\sum_{k \leq n} M_k > n^{1 + c}$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is it true that there exists $c > 0$ such that, for all large $n$, $\sum_{k \leq n} M_k > n^{1 + c}$? The \$100 prize was offered for the third question in [Er97f]. This was resolved by GPT 5.6 and Korsky (see the proof claims), who proved that $\sum_{k\leq n}M_k \gg \frac{n^{5/4}}{\sqrt{\log n}}$ (and hence for infinitely many $n$ we have $M_n> n^{1/4-o(1)}$).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

