@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/146.lean
@decl Erdos146.erdos_146
-- L4DEL: title: If $H$ is bipartite and is $r$-degenerate, that is, every induced subgraph of $H$ has minimum degree $\leq r$, then $$\mathrm{ex}(n;H) \ll n^{2-1/r}.$$ The answer is no
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $H$ is bipartite and is $r$-degenerate, that is, every induced subgraph of $H$ has minimum degree $\leq r$, then $$\mathrm{ex}(n;H) \ll n^{2-1/r}.$$ The answer is no. OpenAI [OpenAI26] give a connected bipartite `2`-degenerate `H` and constants `c, ε > 0` with $\mathrm{ex}(n;H)\geq cn^{3/2+\epsilon}$ for all large `n`, which exceeds the conjectured $n^{2-1/2}=n^{3/2}$. See `erdos_146.variants.two_degenerate_counterexample`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

