@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/154.lean
@decl Erdos154.erdos_154.variants.lindstrom
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: lindstrom
-- L4DEL: intuition: Lindström's result for $A$ itself [Li98], later strengthened by Kolountzakis [Ko99]: for any sequence of Sidon sets $A_k\subseteq\{0,\ldots,N_k\}$ with $N_k\to\infty$ and $\lvert A_k\rvert\sim N_k^{1/2}$, and any modulus $m\geq 2$, the number of elements of $A_k$ congruent to $i\pmod m$, divided by $N_k^{1/2}$, tends to $1/m$ for every residue $i<m$. Well-distribution of $A+A$ (the actual question, `erdos_154`) follows from this using the Sidon property.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

