@decl Erdos162.erdos_162
-- L4DEL: title: Let $\alpha > 0$ and $n \geq 1$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $\alpha > 0$ and $n \geq 1$. Let $F(n,\alpha)$ be the largest $k$ such that there exists some 2-colouring of the edges of $K_n$ in which any induced subgraph $H$ on at least $k$ vertices contains more than $\alpha\binom{|H|}{2}$ many edges of each colour. Prove that for every fixed $0 \leq \alpha \leq 1/2$, as $n \to \infty$, $F(n,\alpha) \sim c_\alpha \log n$ for some constant $c_\alpha$. We require $\alpha < 1/2$: at $\alpha = 1/2$ no colouring works for any `k ≤ n` (see `erdos_162.variants.half`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

