@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/23.lean
@decl Erdos23.erdos_23.variants.n5
-- L4DEL: title: Every triangle-free graph on $25$ vertices can be made bipartite by removing at most $25$ edges
-- L4DEL: intuition: Every triangle-free graph on $25$ vertices can be made bipartite by removing at most $25$ edges. This is the $n = 5$ case of Erdős Problem 23. It follows from the high-density range of Balogh-Clemen-Lidicky together with McKay's complete catalogue of the 23-vertex extremal graphs for bipartization of triangle-free graphs.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/23.lean
@decl Erdos23.erdos_23.variants.n5_tight
-- L4DEL: title: There exists a triangle-free graph on $25$ vertices such that at least $25$ edges must be removed to make it bipartite
-- L4DEL: intuition: There exists a triangle-free graph on $25$ vertices such that at least $25$ edges must be removed to make it bipartite. The balanced blow-up of $C_5$ with five parts of size $5$ witnesses this.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

