-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $2 \leq a_1 \leq a_2 \leq \cdots$ be a monotone sequence with $a_n \to \infty$. Is $\sum_n \frac{d(n)}{a_1 \cdots a_n}$ irrational, where $d(n)$ is the number of divisors of $n$? Solution: True (proved by Erdős and Straus [ErSt71], Lemma 2.2 and Theorem 2.13).
