@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/261.lean
@decl Erdos261.Erdos261Prop
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: Erdos261Prop
-- L4DEL: intuition: A natural number $n$ is said to have property `Erdos261Prop` if there exist $t \ge 2$ pairwise distinct positive integers $a_1, \ldots, a_t$ such that $n / 2^n = \sum_{1 \le k \le t} a_k / 2^{a_k}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/261.lean
@decl Erdos261.erdos_261.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: i
-- L4DEL: intuition: Are there infinitely many positive integers $n$ such that there exist some $t \ge 2$ and distinct integers $a_1, \ldots, a_t \ge 1$ satisfying $$\frac{n}{2^n} = \sum_{1 \le k \le t} \frac{a_k}{2^{a_k}}?$$ In [Er88c], Erdős notes that Cusick had a simple proof that infinitely many such $n$ exist.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/261.lean
@decl Erdos261.erdos_261.parts.ii
