@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/261.lean
@decl Erdos261.erdos_261.variants.borwein_loring
-- L4DEL: title: For every positive integer $m$, if $n = 2^{m+1} - m - 2$, then $$\frac{n}{2^n} = \sum_{n < k \le n + m} \frac{k}{2^k}.$$ This construction is due to Borwein and Loring [BoLo90]
-- L4DEL: intuition: For every positive integer $m$, if $n = 2^{m+1} - m - 2$, then $$\frac{n}{2^n} = \sum_{n < k \le n + m} \frac{k}{2^k}.$$ This construction is due to Borwein and Loring [BoLo90].
