@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/318.lean
@decl Erdos318.erdos_318.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: There exists a set `A` with positive density that does not have property `P₁`
-- L4DEL: intuition: There exists a set `A` with positive density that does not have property `P₁`. #TODO: prove this lemma by assuming `erdos_318.contain_single_even`. The density sits in an existential, so `HasPosDensity` is the *stronger* reading here and weakening it to positive lower density would claim less, which is the opposite of the usual situation for Erdős' "positive density". It also costs nothing: by `erdos_318.variants.contain_single_even` a witness only needs exactly one even element, and the odd numbers together with one even number have density `1 / 2` on the nose.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

