@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/318.lean
@decl Erdos318.erdos_318.variants.contain_single_even
-- L4DEL: title: For any infinite set `A` containing exactly one positive even number, `A` does not have property `P₁`
-- L4DEL: intuition: For any infinite set `A` containing exactly one positive even number, `A` does not have property `P₁`. Sattler [Sa82] credits this observation to Erdős, who presumably found this after [ErGr80]. The element `0` is not counted, since `P₁` ignores it, and the infinitude hypothesis excludes degenerate sets such as `{2}`, on which `P₁` holds vacuously.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

