@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/318.lean
@decl Erdos318.P₁
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: P₁
-- L4DEL: intuition: A set `A : Set ℕ` is said to have property `P₁` if for any nonconstant sequence `f : A → {-1, 1}`, one can always select a finite, nonempty subset `S ⊆ A \ {0}` such that `∑ n ∈ S, fₙ / n = 0`. This is defined in [Sa82b].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/319.lean
@decl Erdos319.erdos_319
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_319
-- L4DEL: intuition: What is the size of the largest $A\subseteq\{1, \dots, N\}$ such that there is a function $\delta : A \to \{-1, 1\}$ such that $$ \sum_{n\in A} \frac{\delta n}{n} = 0 $$ and $$ \sum_{n\in A'}\frac{\delta n}{n} \neq 0 $$ for all non-empty $A'\subsetneq A$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/319.lean
@decl Erdos319.erdos_319.variants.isTheta
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: isTheta
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $c(N)$ be the size of the largest $A\subseteq\{1, \dots, N\}$ such that there is a function $\delta : A \to \{-1, 1\}$ such that $$ \sum_{n\in A} \frac{\delta n}{n} = 0 $$ and $$ \sum_{n\in A'}\frac{\delta n}{n} \neq 0 $$ for all non-empty $A'\subsetneq A$. What is $\Theta(c(N))$? Trivially $c(N) \leq N$, and `erdos_319.variants.lb` gives $c(N) \geq (1 - \frac{1}{e} + o(1))N$, so $c(N) = \Theta(N)$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/319.lean
@decl Erdos319.erdos_319.variants.lb
-- L4DEL: title: Adenwalla has observed that a lower bound (on the maximum size of $A$) of $$ |A| \geq (1 - \frac{1}{e} + o(1))N $$ follows from the main result of Croot [Cr01]
-- L4DEL: intuition: Adenwalla has observed that a lower bound (on the maximum size of $A$) of $$ |A| \geq (1 - \frac{1}{e} + o(1))N $$ follows from the main result of Croot [Cr01]. [Cr01] Croot, III, Ernest S., _On unit fractions with denominators in short intervals_. Acta Arith. (2001), 99-114.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

