@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/321.lean
@decl Erdos321.erdos_321.variants.lower
-- L4DEL: title: Let $R(N)$ be the maximal such size
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $R(N)$ be the maximal such size. Results of Bleicher and Erdős from [BlEr75] and [BlEr76b] imply that $$ \frac{N}{\log N} \prod_{i=3}^{k} \log_i N \le R(N), $$ valid for any $k \ge 4$ with $\log_k N \ge k$ and any $r \ge 1$ with $\log_{2r} N \ge 1$. (In these bounds $\log_i n$ denotes the $i$-fold iterated logarithm.) [BlEr75] Bleicher, M. N. and Erdős, P., _The number of distinct subsums of $\sum \sb{1}\spN\,1/i$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 29-42. [BlEr76b] Bleicher, Michael N. and Erdős, Paul, _Denominators of Egyptian fractions. II_. Illinois J. Math. (1976), 598-613.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/321.lean
@decl Erdos321.erdos_321.variants.upper
-- L4DEL: title: Let $R(N)$ be the maximal such size
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $R(N)$ be the maximal such size. Results of Bleicher and Erdős from [BlEr75] and [BlEr76b] imply that $$ R(N) \le \frac{1}{\log 2} \log_r N \left( \frac{N}{\log N} \prod_{i=3}^{r} \log_i N \right), $$ valid for any $k \ge 4$ with $\log_k N \ge k$ and any $r \ge 1$ with $\log_{2r} N \ge 1$. (In these bounds $\log_i n$ denotes the $i$-fold iterated logarithm.) Since `Real.log` is defined on all of $\mathbb{R}$, the condition $\log_{2r} N \ge 1$ is formalised as $\log_i N \ge 1$ for all $i \le 2r$, which is equivalent to it for the genuine iterated logarithm and ensures that every intermediate iterate is positive. [BlEr75] Bleicher, M. N. and Erdős, P., _The number of distinct subsums of $\sum \sb{1}\spN\,1/i$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 29-42. [BlEr76b] Bleicher, Michael N. and Erdős, Paul, _Denominators of Egyptian fractions. II_. Illinois J. Math. (1976), 598-613.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

