@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/326.lean
@decl Erdos326.erdos_326
-- L4DEL: title: Does there exist $A = \{a_1 < a_2 < \cdots\} \subset \mathbb{N}$ which is a minimal basis of order $2$ (i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: Does there exist $A = \{a_1 < a_2 < \cdots\} \subset \mathbb{N}$ which is a minimal basis of order $2$ (i.e. every large integer is the sum of $2$ elements from $A$, and no proper subset of $A$ has this property), such that $$\lim_{k\to\infty} \frac{a_k}{k^2} = c$$ for some $c \neq 0$? Erdős and Graham conjectured a negative answer to this question [ErGr80]. "Minimal basis of order $2$" is formalised as `Minimal` for the predicate `Set.IsAsymptoticAddBasisOfOrder · 2` on sets of naturals ordered by inclusion.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

