@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/332.lean
@decl Erdos332.erdos_332
-- L4DEL: title: Let $A\subseteq \mathbb{N}$ and $D(A)$ be the set of those numbers which occur infinitely often as $a_1 - a_2$ with $a_1, a_2\in A$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $A\subseteq \mathbb{N}$ and $D(A)$ be the set of those numbers which occur infinitely often as $a_1 - a_2$ with $a_1, a_2\in A$. What conditions on $A$ are sufficient to ensure $D(A)$ has bounded gaps? This is formalised here using the `answer(sorry)` mechanism. In order to solve this problem one has to provide what the sufficient conditions are, and proof that they imply the desired condition. If the condition is a solution to the problem is up to human judgement.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

