@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/348.lean
@decl Erdos348.erdos_348
-- L4DEL: title: For what values of $0 \leq m < n$ is there a complete sequence $A = \{a_1 \leq a_2 \leq \cdots\}$ of integers such that 1
-- L4DEL: intuition: For what values of $0 \leq m < n$ is there a complete sequence $A = \{a_1 \leq a_2 \leq \cdots\}$ of integers such that 1. $A$ remains complete after removing any $m$ elements, but 2. $A$ is not complete after removing any $n$ elements. Geneson [Ge26, Theorem 1] proved that the pairs are exactly those with $m \leq 1$. Completeness allows finitely many exceptions, and deletions remove indexed occurrences.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

