@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/35.lean
@decl Erdos35.erdos_35.variants.plunnecke
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: plunnecke
-- L4DEL: intuition: Plünnecke [Pl70] proved that if $B\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ is an additive basis of order $k$ with $0\in B$ then $d_S(A+B)\geq d_s(A)^{1-1/k}$ for every $A\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ with $d_s(A)>0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

