@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/36.lean
@decl Erdos36.M_one
-- L4DEL: title: This example calculates the value of $M 1$
-- L4DEL: intuition: This example calculates the value of $M 1$. The set is $\{1, 2\}$, so the only partition is $A = \{1\}, B = \{2\}$ (or vice versa). The possible differences are $1 - 2 = -1$ and $2 - 1 = 1$. The `Overlap` for $k=-1$ is 1 (if $A=\{1\}, B=\{2\}$) and for $k=1$ also 1 (if $A=\{2\}, B=\{1\}$ ). The `MaxOverlap` is $1$, since the `Overlap` is $0$ for other $k$. Thus, $M 1 = 1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/36.lean
