-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/36.lean
@decl Erdos36.M_two
-- L4DEL: title: For $n = 2$, the set is $\{1, 2, 3, 4\}$
-- L4DEL: intuition: For $n = 2$, the set is $\{1, 2, 3, 4\}$. The balanced partition $A = \{1, 4\}, B = \{2, 3\}$ has all four pairwise differences ($\pm 1, \pm 2$) distinct, so `MaxOverlap = 1`. Any balanced partition has both pieces nonempty, so `MaxOverlap \geq 1`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

