@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/365.lean
@decl Erdos365.erdos_365.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Do all pairs of consecutive powerful numbers $n$ and $n+1$ come from solutions to Pell equations?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Do all pairs of consecutive powerful numbers $n$ and $n+1$ come from solutions to Pell equations? In other words, must either $n$ or $n+1$ be a square? The answer to the first question is no: Golomb [Go70] observed that both $12167=23^3$ and $12168=2^3 3^2 13^2$ are powerful. We require $n>0$ since `Nat.Powerful` also includes $0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

