@decl Erdos367.erdos_367.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Let $B_2(n)$ be the $2$-full part of $n$ (that is, $B_2(n)=n/n'$ where $n'$ is the product of all primes that divide $n$ exactly once)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $B_2(n)$ be the $2$-full part of $n$ (that is, $B_2(n)=n/n'$ where $n'$ is the product of all primes that divide $n$ exactly once). Is it true that, for every fixed $k \geq 1$, $\prod_{n \leq m < n+k} B_2(m) \ll n^{2+o(1)}$?
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/367.lean
@decl Erdos367.erdos_367.parts.ii
