@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/375.lean
@decl Erdos375.erdos_375.variants.log
-- L4DEL: title: There exists a constant `c > 0` such that for all `n`, if `k < c * (log n / (log (log n))) ^ 3 → (∀ i < k, ¬ (n + i + 1).Prime)`, then there are distinct primes `p₁,
-- L4DEL: intuition: There exists a constant `c > 0` such that for all `n`, if `k < c * (log n / (log (log n))) ^ 3 → (∀ i < k, ¬ (n + i + 1).Prime)`, then there are distinct primes `p₁, ... pₖ` such that `pᵢ ∣ n + i` for all `1 ≤ i ≤ k`. This is proved in [RST75]. There is no need to only consider sufficiently large `n` because one can always take `c` small enough so that `k < c * (log n / (log (log n))) ^ 3` implies that `k = 0` until `n` is large.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

