@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/377.lean
@decl Erdos377.erdos_377.variants.ae
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: ae
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdos, Graham, Ruzsa, and Straus proved that if $$ f(n) = \sum_{p \leq n} 1_{p\nmid {2n \choose n}}\frac{1}{p} $$ and $$ \gamma_0 = \sum_{k = 2}^{\infty} \frac{\log k}{2^k} $$ then for almost all integers $f(m) = \gamma_0 + o(1)$, i.e. for every $\varepsilon > 0$ the set of $n$ with $|f(n) - \gamma_0| < \varepsilon$ has natural density one. [EGRS75] Erdős, P. and Graham, R. L. and Ruzsa, I. Z. and Straus, E. G., _On the prime factors of $\binom{2n}{n}$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 83-92.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/377.lean
@decl Erdos377.erdos_377.variants.limit.i
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: i
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdos, Graham, Ruzsa, and Straus proved that if $$ f(n) = \sum_{p \leq n} 1_{p\nmid {2n \choose n}}\frac{1}{p} $$ and $$ \gamma_0 = \sum_{k = 2}^{\infty} \frac{\log k}{2^k} $$ then $$ \lim_{x\to\infty} \frac{1}{x}\sum_{n\leq x} f(n) = \gamma_0 $$ [EGRS75] Erdős, P. and Graham, R. L. and Ruzsa, I. Z. and Straus, E. G., _On the prime factors of $\binom{2n}{n}$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 83-92.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/377.lean
@decl Erdos377.erdos_377.variants.limit.ii
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: ii
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdos, Graham, Ruzsa, and Straus proved that if $$ f(n) = \sum_{p \leq n} 1_{p\nmid {2n \choose n}}\frac{1}{p} $$ and $$ \gamma_0 = \sum_{k = 2}^{\infty} \frac{\log k}{2^k} $$ then $$ \lim_{x\to\infty} \frac{1}{x}\sum_{n\leq x} f(n)^2 = \gamma_0^2 $$ [EGRS75] Erdős, P. and Graham, R. L. and Ruzsa, I. Z. and Straus, E. G., _On the prime factors of $\binom{2n}{n}$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 83-92.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/377.lean
@decl Erdos377.erdos_377.variants.ub
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: ub
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdos, Graham, Ruzsa, and Straus proved that if $$ f(n) = \sum_{p \leq n} 1_{p\nmid {2n \choose n}}\frac{1}{p} $$ then there is some constant $c < 1$ such that for all large $n$ $$ f(n) \leq c \log\log n. $$ [EGRS75] Erdős, P. and Graham, R. L. and Ruzsa, I. Z. and Straus, E. G., _On the prime factors of $\binom{2n}{n}$_. Math. Comp. (1975), 83-92.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

