@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/384.lean
@decl Erdos384.erdos_384
-- L4DEL: title: If $1k^2$ the binomial coefficient $\binom{n}{k}$ is divisible by a prime $p<n/k$
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $1k^2$ the binomial coefficient $\binom{n}{k}$ is divisible by a prime $p<n/k$. Discussed in problem B31 and B33 of Guy's collection [Gu04]. Stronger forms of this conjecture are 1094 and 1095. Ecklund's theorem is stated for $n \geq 2k$ with the single exception $\binom{7}{3}$; by the symmetry $\binom{n}{k} = \binom{n}{n-k}$ this is the form above, where $\binom{7}{4}$ is the second exception. The prime bound is $p \leq n/2$ (that is, $2p \leq n$); see `erdos_384.variants.strict` for the strict inequality.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

