@decl Erdos399.erdos_399.variants.sum_two_squares
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: sum_two_squares
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős and Obláth observed that the Bertrand-style fact (first proved by Breusch [Br32]) that, if $q_i$ is the sequence of primes congruent to $3\pmod{4}$ then $q_{i+1}<2q_i$ except for $q_1=3$, together with Fermat's theorem on the sums of two squares implies that the only solution to $n!=x^2+y^2$ is $6!=12^2+24^2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

