@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/40.lean
@decl Erdos40.erdos_40.variants.weaker
-- L4DEL: title: Is there any function $g(N) → \infty$ such that $$\lvert A\cap \{1,\ldots,N\}\rvert \gg \frac{N^{1/2}}{g(N)}$$ implies $\limsup 1_A\ast 1_A(n)=\infty$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is there any function $g(N) → \infty$ such that $$\lvert A\cap \{1,\ldots,N\}\rvert \gg \frac{N^{1/2}}{g(N)}$$ implies $\limsup 1_A\ast 1_A(n)=\infty$? This is a weaker form of Erdős Problem 40, which asks for all such $g$. Establishing the implication for even one $g(N) → \infty$ already answers Erdős Problem 28 positively, because a basis of order $2$ satisfies $\lvert A\cap \{1,\ldots,N\}\rvert \gg N^{1/2}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

