-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős and Graham [ErGr80] ask this allowing $p=2$, but this is presumably an oversight, since clearly there are infinitely many solutions when $p=2$. Observe that this creates $1! + a = 2^k$. For all $k$, fix $a = 2^k - 1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/405.lean
