@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/418.lean
@decl Erdos418.erdos_418.variants.sigma
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: sigma
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős [Er73b] has shown that a positive density set of natural numbers cannot be written as $\sigma(n)-n$ (numbers not of this form are called nonaliquot, or sometimes untouchable). Here "positive density" means positive lower density: Banks and Luca [BaLu05] proved that the set of nonaliquots has lower density at least $1/48$, Chen and Zhao [ChZh11] improved this to $0.06$, and it is not known whether the natural density of the nonaliquots exists (Pollack and Pomerance [PoPo16] give a heuristic predicting its value).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

