@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/422.lean
@decl Erdos422.IsHofstadterQ
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsHofstadterQ
-- L4DEL: intuition: `IsHofstadterQ f` means that $f$ is Hofstadter's $Q$-sequence (OEIS A005185): $f(1) = f(2) = 1$ and for $n > 2$ $$ f(n) = f(n - f(n - 1)) + f(n - f(n - 2)), $$ where the recurrence requires $f(n - 1) < n$ and $f(n - 2) < n$, so that both arguments on the right-hand side are positive integers. The sequence begins $1, 1, 2, 3, 3, 4, \ldots$. At most one function satisfies this predicate. Some function satisfies it if and only if $f(n)$ is well-defined for all $n$, which is not known.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

