@decl Erdos427.erdos_427.variants.shiu
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: shiu
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Shiu's theorem**: for any $k \geq 1$ and $(a, q) = 1$ there exist infinitely many $k$-tuples of consecutive primes $p_m, \dots, p_{m + k - 1}$ all of which are congruent to $a$ modulo $q$. This is stated ahead of `erdos_427` because the formal proof linked there assumes it, and the `assuming` clause must name a declaration that already exists. [Sh00] Shiu, D. K. L., _Strings of congruent primes_. J. London Math. Soc. (2) (2000), 359-373.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

