@decl Erdos43.erdos_43.parts.ii
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: ii
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $A$ and $B$ are equal-sized Sidon sets in $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ with $(A-A)\cap(B-B)=\{0\}$, can the bound be improved to $$\binom{\lvert A\rvert}{2}+\binom{\lvert B\rvert}{2} \leq (1-c+o(1))\binom{f(N)}{2}$$ for some constant $c>0$? The answer is no; the Erdős Problems page records a negative answer due to Barreto.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

