@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/430.lean
@decl Erdos430.terms
-- L4DEL: title: The terms of the sequence of Erdős Problem 430 for a given $n$: the integers $m$ with $1 < m < n$ all of whose prime factors are $> n - m$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The terms of the sequence of Erdős Problem 430 for a given $n$: the integers $m$ with $1 < m < n$ all of whose prime factors are $> n - m$. The decreasing sequence $a_1 > a_2 > \cdots$ of the problem lists the elements of this set in decreasing order: $a_1 = n - 1$ is its largest element and $a_k$ is its largest element below $a_{k-1}$. The integer $1$ has no prime factors and is not a term of the sequence, which stops instead, as in the example on erdosproblems.com: for $n = 8$ the sequence is $7, 5$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

