@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/442.lean
@decl Erdos442.Set.bddProdUpper
-- L4DEL: title: If `A` be a set of natural numbers and let `x` be real, then `A.bddProdUpper x` is the finite upper-triangular set of pairs of elements of `A` that are `≤ x`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `A` be a set of natural numbers and let `x` be real, then `A.bddProdUpper x` is the finite upper-triangular set of pairs of elements of `A` that are `≤ x`. Specifically, it is the set `{(n, m) | n ∈ A, n ≤ x, m ∈ A, m ≤ x, n < m}`
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

