@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/445.lean
@decl Erdos445.erdos_445
-- L4DEL: title: Is it true that, for any $c>1/2$, if $p$ is a sufficiently large prime then, for any $n\geq 0$, there exist $a,b\in(n,n+p^c)$ such that $ab\equiv 1\pmod{p}$?
