-- L4DEL: intuition: Taking $n$ to be the product of primes between $\log n$ and $(2 + o(1)) \log n$ gives an example where $$ q(n, \log n) \ge (2 + o(1)) \log n. $$ Can one prove that $q(n, \log n) < (1 - \epsilon) (\log n)^2$ for all large $n$ and some $\epsilon > 0$?
