@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/457.lean
@decl Erdos457.erdos_457.variants.qnk
-- L4DEL: title: More generally, let $q(n, k)$ denote the least prime which does not divide $\prod_{1 \le i \le k}(n + i)$
-- L4DEL: intuition: More generally, let $q(n, k)$ denote the least prime which does not divide $\prod_{1 \le i \le k}(n + i)$. This problem asks whether $q(n, \log n) \ge (2 + \epsilon) \log n$ infinitely often. This follows from `erdos_457`: if every prime $p \le (2 + \epsilon) \log n$ divides $\prod_{1 \le i \le \log n} (n + i)$, then $q(n, \log n)$, the least prime not dividing this product, must exceed $(2 + \epsilon) \log n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

