@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/459.lean
@decl Erdos459.erdos_459
-- L4DEL: title: Let $f(u)$ be the largest $v$ such that no $m\in (u,v)$ is composed entirely of primes dividing $uv$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $f(u)$ be the largest $v$ such that no $m\in (u,v)$ is composed entirely of primes dividing $uv$. Estimate $f(u)$. The estimate $u + 2 \le f(u) \le u^2$ holds for every $u \ge 2$. The upper bound is attained when $u$ is prime, and the lower bound when $u = 2^k - 2$ with $k \ge 2$; Cambie further showed that $f(n) = (1 + o(1))n$ for almost all $n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/459.lean
@decl Erdos459.erdos_459.variants.upper_tight
-- L4DEL: title: The upper bound $f u ≤ u ^ 2$ is attained exactly when `u` is prime: $f p = p ^ 2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The upper bound $f u ≤ u ^ 2$ is attained exactly when `u` is prime: $f p = p ^ 2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/459.lean
@decl Erdos459.f
-- L4DEL: title: The function from the problem, in its equivalent form: `f u` is the smallest `v > u` all of whose prime factors divide `u`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The function from the problem, in its equivalent form: `f u` is the smallest `v > u` all of whose prime factors divide `u`. (Equivalently, `f u` is the largest `v` such that no `m ∈ (u, v)` is composed entirely of primes dividing `u * v`.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

