-- L4DEL: intuition: Does every finite colouring of the integers have a monochromatic solution to $1=\sum \frac{1}{n_i}$ with $2\leq n_1<\cdots <n_k$? The answer is yes, as proved by Croot [Cr03] - indeed, there are infinitely many disjoint such monochromatic solutions.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

