-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $p(n)$ denote the least prime factor of $n$. Is there a constant $C>0$ such that $$\sum_{x\leq n\leq x+C\sqrt{x}(\log x)^2}\frac{p(n)}{n}\gg 1$$ for all sufficiently large $x$?
