@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/470.lean
@decl Erdos470.erdos_470.variants.weird_pos_density
-- L4DEL: title: Benkoski and Erdős BeEr74 proved that the set of weird numbers has positive density
-- L4DEL: intuition: Benkoski and Erdős BeEr74 proved that the set of weird numbers has positive density. `HasPosDensity` is the right reading here, rather than the positive *lower* density that Erdős' "positive density" usually abbreviates. Their Theorem 5 is stated as "the density of weird numbers is positive", and they first establish that the density exists at all: "It is clear that the weird numbers have a density since both the abundant numbers and the pseudoperfect numbers have a density. (A weird number is abundant and not pseudoperfect.)" The work in the paper goes into showing that density is not `0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

