-- L4DEL: intuition: Segal also asked whether for every $n \ge 2$ there is a permutation $a_1, \ldots, a_n$ of $\{1, \ldots, n\}$ such that $a_k + a_{k+1}$ is prime for all $1 \le k < n$. This is conjectured to be true, and has been verified for infinitely many $n$.
