@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/484.lean
@decl Erdos484.erdos_484
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_484
-- L4DEL: intuition: Prove that there exists an absolute constant $c>0$ such that, whenever $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ is $k$-coloured (and $N$ is large enough depending on $k$) then there are at least $cN$ many integers in $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ which are representable as a monochromatic sum (that is, $a+b$ where $a,b\in \{1,\ldots,N\}$ are in the same colour class and $a\neq b$). A conjecture of Roth. Solved by Erdős, Sárközy, and Sós [ESS89], who in fact prove that there are at least $\frac{N}{2}-O(N^{1-1/2^{k+1}})$ many even numbers which are of this form.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

