-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_488
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $A$ be a finite set and $$B=\{ n \geq 1 : a\mid n\textrm{ for some }a\in A\}.$$ Is it true that, for every $m>n\geq \max(A)$, $$\frac{\lvert B\cap [1,m]\rvert }{m}< 2\frac{\lvert B\cap [1,n]\rvert}{n}?$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/489.lean
@decl Erdos489.erdos_489
-- L4DEL: title: Let $A\subseteq \mathbb{N}$ be a set such that $\lvert A\cap [1,x]\rvert=o(x^{1/2})$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $A\subseteq \mathbb{N}$ be a set such that $\lvert A\cap [1,x]\rvert=o(x^{1/2})$. Let $B=\{ n\geq 1 : a\nmid n\textrm{ for all }a\in A\}$. If $B=\{b_1 < b_2 < \cdots\}$ then is it true that $$\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{1}{x}\sum_{b_i < x}(b_{i+1}-b_i)^2$$ exists (and is finite)? For example, when $A=\{p^2: p\textrm{ prime}\}$ then $B$ is the set of squarefree numbers, and the existence of this limit was proved by Erdős. See also [208].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/489.lean
@decl Erdos489.erdos_489.variants.squarefree
