-- L4DEL: intuition: Selfridge and Straus [SeSt58] showed that the conjecture is true when $k = 2$ and $|A| \ne 2^l$ for $l \ge 0$. They also gave counterexamples when $k = 2$ and $|A| = 2^l$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/494.lean
@decl Erdos494.erdos_494.variants.k_eq_3_card_gt_6
-- L4DEL: title: Selfridge and Straus [SeSt58] also showed that the conjecture is true when 1) $k = 3$ and $|A| > 6$, except possibly for $|A| = 27$ and $|A| = 486$, or 2) $k = 4$ and $|A| > 12$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Selfridge and Straus [SeSt58] also showed that the conjecture is true when 1) $k = 3$ and $|A| > 6$, except possibly for $|A| = 27$ and $|A| = 486$, or 2) $k = 4$ and $|A| > 12$. More generally, they proved that $A$ is determined by $A_k$ (and $|A|$) if $|A|$ is divisible by a prime greater than $k$. The cases $|A| = 27$ and $|A| = 486$ were left open in [SeSt58]. Fomin and Izhboldin [FoIz94] later found two distinct sets of each of these sizes with the same multiset of $3$-sums, so these exceptions are genuine.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

