@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/522.lean
@decl Erdos522.KacCoefficients
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: KacCoefficients
-- L4DEL: intuition: A sequence of *Kac coefficients* over a subset `S` of a field `k` is a countably infinite sequence of independent random variables, each uniformly distributed over `S` with respect to the reference measure `μ`. The default reference measure is the counting measure, so that for a finite set `S` each coefficient takes every value of `S` with probability `1 / |S|`. Such a sequence determines a *Kac polynomial* of degree `n` for each `n`, which is the random polynomial given by `KacCoefficients.polynomial`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

