-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős and Szemerédi [ErSz83] proved that there exist arbitrarily large sets $A$ such that the number of integers which are the sum or product of distinct elements of $A$ is at most $$\exp\left(c \frac{(\log \lvert A\rvert)^2}{\log\log\lvert A\rvert}\right)$$ for some constant $c>0$. (erdosproblems.com multiplies by $\log\log\lvert A\rvert$; [ErSz83, Theorem 2] divides by it.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

