@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/535.lean
@decl Erdos535.erdos_535
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_535
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $r \geq 3$, and let $f_r(N)$ denote the size of the largest subset of $\{1,\ldots,N\}$ such that no subset of size $r$ has the same pairwise greatest common divisor between all elements. Erdős [Er64] proved that $f_3(N) > N^{c/\log\log N}$ for some constant $c > 0$, and conjectured this should also be an upper bound; here we state the conjectural upper bound for all $r \geq 3$. See also [536].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

