@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/549.lean
@decl Erdos549.erdos_549
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_549
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $T$ is a tree which is a bipartite graph with $k$ vertices in one class and $2k$ vertices in the other class then $$R(T)=4k-1.$$ This is false: Norin, Sun, and Zhao [NSZ16] have proved that if $T$ is the union of two stars on $k$ and $2k$ vertices, with an edge joining the centre of the two stars, then $R(T)\geq (4.2-o(1))k$, and conjectured that $R(T)=(4.2+o(1))k$. This problem is #15 in Ramsey Theory in the graphs problem collection.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

