-- L4DEL: intuition: $F(n,\alpha)$ is the smallest $m$ such that there exists a 2-coloring of the edges of $K_n$ so that every $X\subseteq [n]$ with $|X|\geq m$ contains more than $\alpha\binom{|X|}{2}$ edges of each color.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/563.lean
@decl Erdos563.HasBalancedSubsets
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasBalancedSubsets
-- L4DEL: intuition: A 2-coloring of $K_n$ (represented by graph $G$ on $\mathrm{Fin}\; n$) is balanced on subsets of size at least $m$ with parameter $\alpha$ if every $X \subseteq [n]$ with $|X| \geq m$ contains more than $\alpha \binom{|X|}{2}$ edges of each color.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

