@decl Erdos566.erdos_566
-- L4DEL: title: Let $G$ be such that any subgraph on $k$ vertices has at most $2k-3$ edges
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $G$ be such that any subgraph on $k$ vertices has at most $2k-3$ edges. Is it true that, if $H$ has $m$ edges and no isolated vertices, then $R(G,H) \ll m$? In other words: if $G$ is sparse (every induced subgraph on $k$ vertices has $≤ 2k-3$ edges), is $G$ Ramsey size linear?
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

