@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/579.lean
@decl Erdos579.erdos_579
-- L4DEL: title: Let $\delta > 0$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $\delta > 0$. If $n$ is sufficiently large and $G$ is a graph on $n$ vertices with no $K_{2,2,2}$ (the octahedron) and at least $\delta n^2$ edges, must $G$ contain an independent set of size $\gg_\delta n$? This is a problem of Erdős, Hajnal, Sós, and Szemerédi [EHSS83]. It is **open**; they proved the statement for $\delta > 1/8$ (see `erdos_579.variants.ehss_large_delta`), and the difficulty is to push the edge-density threshold down to an arbitrary $\delta > 0$. Here $K_{2,2,2}$ is the complete tripartite graph with all parts of size $2$, encoded as `completeMultipartiteGraph (fun _ : Fin 3 => Fin 2)`; "contains no $K_{2,2,2}$" is expressed via `SimpleGraph.Free`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/579.lean
@decl Erdos579.erdos_579.variants.ehss_large_delta
-- L4DEL: title: The partial result of Erdős, Hajnal, Sós, and Szemerédi [EHSS83]: the statement of `erdos_579` holds whenever the edge-density coefficient exceeds $1/8$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The partial result of Erdős, Hajnal, Sós, and Szemerédi [EHSS83]: the statement of `erdos_579` holds whenever the edge-density coefficient exceeds $1/8$. That is, for every $\delta > 1/8$ there is a $c > 0$ such that for all sufficiently large $n$, every $K_{2,2,2}$-free graph $G$ on $n$ vertices with at least $\delta n^2$ edges has an independent set of size at least $c n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/579.lean
@decl Erdos579.erdos_579.variants.octahedron_not_free
