-- L4DEL: intuition: Katz and Tardos [KaTa04] proved that some point of $A$ has $\gg n^{c-o(1)}$ distinct distances to the other points of $A$, where $$c=\frac{48-14e}{55-16e}=0.864137\cdots.$$
