@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/604.lean
@decl Erdos604.pinnedDistinctDistances
-- L4DEL: title: The pinned distance function $f(n)$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The pinned distance function $f(n)$. For a set $A$ of $n$ points in $\mathbb{R}^2$, take the largest number of distinct distances from a point $x \in A$ to the other points of $A$. Then $f(n)$ is the least such value over all such sets $A$. The distance $d(x, x) = 0$ is not counted, as in `distinctDistancesFrom`. Every $n$ admits a set of $n$ points in $\mathbb{R}^2$, so the infimum is a minimum.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

