-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/627.lean
@decl Erdos627.maxChromaticCliqueRatio
-- L4DEL: title: `maxChromaticCliqueRatio n` is $f(n)$, the maximum of $\chi(G)/\omega(G)$ over all graphs $G$ on $n$ vertices
-- L4DEL: intuition: `maxChromaticCliqueRatio n` is $f(n)$, the maximum of $\chi(G)/\omega(G)$ over all graphs $G$ on $n$ vertices. A graph on `Fin n` is finite, so its chromatic number (an element of `ℕ∞`) is finite and `ENat.toNat` returns it. The maximum is taken over the finitely many graphs on `Fin n`, so the supremum is attained. For $n = 0$ the only graph is empty, with $\chi = \omega = 0$, and the convention $0 / 0 = 0$ gives $f(0) = 0$; this does not affect any asymptotic statement below.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

