-- L4DEL: intuition: The version of the problem where the $o(1)$ term must be uniform in the dimension $d$ has a negative answer. This follows from `Erdos670.erdos_670.variants.ho` (Ho [Ho26]).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/670.lean
@decl Erdos670.HasSeparatedDistances
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasSeparatedDistances
-- L4DEL: intuition: A finite set $A$ of points has *separated distances* if all its pairwise distances differ by at least $1$: for any two different unordered pairs $\{a, b\} \neq \{c, e\}$ of distinct points of $A$, we have $\lvert d(a, b) - d(c, e)\rvert \geq 1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

