-- L4DEL: intuition: Alexeev and Mixon [arxiv/2510.19804] have disproved this conjecture, showing that $\{1, 2, 4, 8, 13\}$ cannot be extended to any perfect difference set modulo a positive integer. The modulus `0` is excluded, as in `erdos_707`: `IsPerfectDifferenceSet B 0` describes an infinite perfect difference set in `ℤ`, and every finite Sidon set extends to one.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

