@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/732.lean
@decl Erdos732.erdos_732.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: i
-- L4DEL: intuition: Call a sequence $1< X_1\leq \cdots \leq X_m\leq n$ block-compatible if there is a pairwise balanced block design $A_1,\ldots,A_m\subseteq \{1,\ldots,n\}$ such that $\lvert A_i\rvert=X_i$ for $1\leq i\leq m$. (A pairwise block design means that every pair in $\{1,\ldots,n\}$ is contained in exactly one of the $A_i$.) Are there necessary and sufficient conditions for $(X_i)$ to be block-compatible? Is there some constant $c>0$ such that for all large $n$ there are $$\geq \exp(c n^{1/2}\log n)$$ many block-compatible sequences for $\{1,\ldots,n\}$?
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/732.lean
@decl Erdos732.erdos_732.parts.ii
-- L4DEL: title: Is there some constant $c>0$ such that for all large $n$ there are at least $\exp(c n^{1/2}\log n)$ block-compatible sequences?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is there some constant $c>0$ such that for all large $n$ there are at least $\exp(c n^{1/2}\log n)$ block-compatible sequences? Alon has proved there are at least $2^{(\frac{1}{2}+o(1))n^{1/2}\log n}$ many sequences which are block-compatible for $n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

