@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/742.lean
@decl Erdos742.erdos_742
-- L4DEL: title: Murty-Simon Conjecture** Let $G$ be a graph on $n$ vertices with diameter $2$ such that deleting any edge increases the diameter
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Murty-Simon Conjecture** Let $G$ be a graph on $n$ vertices with diameter $2$ such that deleting any edge increases the diameter. Is it true that $G$ has at most $\lfloor n^2 / 4 \rfloor$ edges? Equality is conjectured to hold for the complete balanced bipartite graph $K_{\lceil n/2 \rceil, \lfloor n/2 \rfloor}$. The conjecture is resolved up to a finite check: Fan [Fa87] verified it for $n \leq 24$ and $n = 26$, and Füredi [Fü92] proved it for all sufficiently large $n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

