@decl Erdos750.erdos_750.variants.stiebitz
-- L4DEL: title: Stiebitz's theorem** [St85]: every graph in $M_r$ has chromatic number at least $r$
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Stiebitz's theorem** [St85]: every graph in $M_r$ has chromatic number at least $r$. The matching upper bound follows from the construction, so the chromatic number is exactly $r$. This is stated ahead of `erdos_750` because the formal proof linked there assumes it, and the `assuming` clause must name a declaration that already exists. See also [SaSt89] and [MuSt19].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

