@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/750.lean
@decl Erdos750.IsRecursivelyBuiltMr
-- L4DEL: title: `G` belongs to the class $M_r$, meaning it is built from $K_2$ by $r - 2$ generalised Mycielskians
-- L4DEL: intuition: `G` belongs to the class $M_r$, meaning it is built from $K_2$ by $r - 2$ generalised Mycielskians. Stiebitz's theorem is about this class and not about arbitrary graphs: it is false that $\chi(M_s(H)) = \chi(H) + 1$ for every $H$ and every $s$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/750.lean
@decl Erdos750.MycAdj
-- L4DEL: title: Adjacency of the generalised Mycielskian, before `SimpleGraph.fromRel` packages it as a graph
-- L4DEL: intuition: Adjacency of the generalised Mycielskian, before `SimpleGraph.fromRel` packages it as a graph. Two level-`0` vertices are adjacent when the underlying vertices are; a level-`i` vertex and a level-`i + 1` vertex are adjacent when the underlying vertices are; and the apex is adjacent to every vertex on the top level. The relation is already symmetric and irreflexive, so `fromRel` changes nothing about it.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

