-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős [Er93] conjectured that $\mathrm{ex}(n; C_4) = \frac{n^{3/2}}{2} + \frac n4 + O(n^{1/2})$ for all $n$, having proved the upper bound $\mathrm{ex}(n; C_4) \le \frac{n^{3/2}}{2} + \frac n4 + O(n^{1/2})$ in [Er75]. This is false: Ma and Yang [MaYa23] proved that, for some absolute constant $c > 0$ and a positive density set of $n$, $\mathrm{ex}(n; C_4) \le \frac{n^{3/2}}{2} + (\frac14 - c) n$.
