-- L4DEL: intuition: We call $A$ proportionately dissociated if every finite $B\subset A$ contains a dissociated set of size $\gg \lvert B\rvert$. In other words, there is a (global) $c > 0$ such that every finite $B \subset A$ contains a dissociated set of size $\geq c|B|$.
