@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/78.lean
@decl Erdos78.explicitGraph
-- L4DEL: title: The graph on `Fin n` described by an adjacency oracle `adj`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The graph on `Fin n` described by an adjacency oracle `adj`. Two distinct vertices `u` and `v` are adjacent if `adj (1ⁿ, u, v)` or `adj (1ⁿ, v, u)` is `true`. The number of vertices is given in unary, as the list `List.replicate n true`. So if `adj` is computable in polynomial time, then the whole graph on `n` vertices is computable in time polynomial in `n`. This is the notion of a *weakly explicit* family of graphs; compare `stronglyExplicitGraph`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/78.lean
@decl Erdos78.NoHomogeneousSet
