-- L4DEL: intuition: Chen and Fang [ChFa10] proved the stronger statement that $A(x)B(x)-x\to \infty$ if $A$ and $B$ are infinite sets such that $A+B$ contains all large integers and $$\limsup_{x\to \infty}\frac{A(x)B(x)}{x}<\frac{5}{4}.$$ They later [ChFa14] improved $5/4$ to $3-\sqrt{3}\approx 1.268$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

