@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/786.lean
@decl Erdos786.erdos_786.parts.i.selfridge
-- L4DEL: title: Let $\epsilon > 0$ be given
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $\epsilon > 0$ be given. Then, for a sufficiently large prime `p`, take the sequence of consecutive primes $p_1 < \cdots < p_k$ such that $$ \sum_{i=1}^k \frac{1}{p_i} < 1 < \sum_{i=1}^{k + 1} \frac{1}{p_i}, $$ and let $A$ be the set of all naturals divisible by exactly one of $p_1, ..., p_k$ (with multiplicity $1$). Then $A$ has density $> \frac{1}{e} - \epsilon$ and has the property that $a_1\cdots a_r = b_1\cdots b_s$ with $a_i, b_j\in A$ can only hold when $r = s$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

