@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/80.lean
@decl Erdos80.erdos_80.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: i
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $c>0$ and let $f_c(n)$ be the maximal $m$ such that every graph $G$ with $n$ vertices and at least $cn^2$ edges, where each edge is contained in at least one triangle, must contain a book of size $m$, that is, an edge shared by at least $m$ different triangles. Estimate $f_c(n)$. In particular, is it true that $f_c(n)>n^\epsilon$ for some $\epsilon>0$? The answer is no. Fox and Loh [FoLo12] proved that $f_c(n) \leq n^{O(1/\log\log n)}$ for every fixed $c < 1/4$, so no $\epsilon > 0$ works for, say, $c = 1/8$. For $c > 1/4$ the situation is different: $f_c(n) \geq n/6$, see erdosproblems.com/80. The bound $c < 1/2$ is what makes the hypothesis satisfiable: a simple graph on $n$ vertices has at most $n(n-1)/2$ edges, so no graph has $cn^2$ of them once $c \geq 1/2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/80.lean
@decl Erdos80.erdos_80.parts.ii
-- L4DEL: title: The weaker question from the same problem: is $f_c(n) \gg \log n$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: The weaker question from the same problem: is $f_c(n) \gg \log n$? Same feasibility bound on `c` as above.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/80.lean
@decl Erdos80.EveryEdgeInTriangle
-- L4DEL: title: Every edge of `G` lies in at least one triangle
-- L4DEL: intuition: Every edge of `G` lies in at least one triangle.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/80.lean
@decl Erdos80.everyEdgeInTriangle_bot
-- L4DEL: title: `EveryEdgeInTriangle` holds vacuously on a graph with no edges, so the admissible set is nonempty only through the edge count
