@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/80.lean
@decl Erdos80.f
-- L4DEL: title: $f_c(n)$, the largest book size forced on every admissible graph, which is the least book number among them
-- L4DEL: intuition: $f_c(n)$, the largest book size forced on every admissible graph, which is the least book number among them. `sInf` of the empty set is `0`, so `f c n = 0` when no graph on `n` vertices has $cn^2$ edges at all. A simple graph has at most $n(n-1)/2$ edges, so that happens for every `n` once $c \geq 1/2$. The statements below therefore restrict `c` to the feasible range; without that they are false at, say, `c = 2` for reasons unrelated to the question.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/800.lean
@decl Erdos800.erdos_800
-- L4DEL: title: If $G$ is a graph on $n$ vertices which has no two adjacent vertices of degree $\geq 3$ then $$R(G)\ll n,$$ where the implied constant is absolute
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $G$ is a graph on $n$ vertices which has no two adjacent vertices of degree $\geq 3$ then $$R(G)\ll n,$$ where the implied constant is absolute. A problem of Burr and Erdős. Solved in the affirmative by Alon [Al94].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/803.lean
@decl Erdos803.erdos_803.variants.alon
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: alon
-- L4DEL: intuition: Alon [Al08] proved that for every $D>1$ and large $n$ there is a graph $G$ with $n$ vertices and $\geq n\log n$ edges such that if $H$ is a $D$-balanced subgraph on $m$ vertices then $H$ has $\ll m\sqrt{\log m}+\log D$ many edges.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/803.lean
@decl Erdos803.erdos_803.variants.janzer_sudakov
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: janzer_sudakov
-- L4DEL: intuition: Janzer and Sudakov [JaSu23] have proved that, for any $k$, if $n$ is sufficiently large then any graph on $n$ vertices with at least $n\log n$ edges contains a $O(1)$-balanced subgraph on $m\geq k$ vertices with $\gg_k \frac{\sqrt{\log m}}{(\log\log m)^{3/2}}m$ many edges.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

