@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/813.lean
@decl Erdos813.erdos_813
-- L4DEL: title: Let $h(n)$ be minimal such that every graph on $n$ vertices where every set of $7$ vertices contains a triangle must contain a clique on at least $h(n)$ vertices
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $h(n)$ be minimal such that every graph on $n$ vertices where every set of $7$ vertices contains a triangle must contain a clique on at least $h(n)$ vertices. Estimate $h(n)$. In particular, do there exist constants $c_1, c_2 > 0$ such that $$n^{1/3+c_1} \ll h(n) \ll n^{1/2-c_2}?$$ The lower half has a positive answer (`Erdos813.erdos_813.variants.lower`); the upper half is `Erdos813.erdos_813.variants.upper`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

