@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/830.lean
@decl Erdos830.erdos_830.variants.pomerance
-- L4DEL: title: We say that $a,b\in \mathbb{N}$ are an amicable pair if $\sigma(a)=\sigma(b)=a+b$
-- L4DEL: intuition: We say that $a,b\in \mathbb{N}$ are an amicable pair if $\sigma(a)=\sigma(b)=a+b$. If $A(x)$ counts the number of amicable $1\leq a\leq b\leq x$ then one can show that $A(x) \leq x \exp(-(\log x)^{1/3})$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/830.lean
@decl Erdos830.erdos_830.variants.pomerance_stronger
-- L4DEL: title: We say that $a,b\in \mathbb{N}$ are an amicable pair if $\sigma(a)=\sigma(b)=a+b$
-- L4DEL: intuition: We say that $a,b\in \mathbb{N}$ are an amicable pair if $\sigma(a)=\sigma(b)=a+b$. If $A(x)$ counts the number of amicable $1\leq a\leq b\leq x$ then one can show that $A(x) \leq x \exp(-(\tfrac{1}{2}+o(1))(\log x\log\log\log x)^{1/2})$. (erdosproblems.com has $\log\log x$; [Po15, Theorem 1.1] has $\log\log\log x$.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/832.lean
@decl Erdos832.erdos_832
-- L4DEL: title: Let $r\geq 3$ and $k$ be sufficiently large in terms of $r$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $r\geq 3$ and $k$ be sufficiently large in terms of $r$. Is it true that every $r$-uniform hypergraph with chromatic number $k$ has at least $$\binom{(r-1)(k-1)+1}{r}$$ edges, with equality only for the complete graph on $(r-1)(k-1)+1$ vertices? This was disproved by Alon [Al85]. The validity of this conjecture for $r=3$ remains open.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/833.lean
@decl Erdos833.erdos_833
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_833
-- L4DEL: intuition: Does there exist an absolute constant $c>0$ such that, for all $r\geq 2$, in any $r$-uniform hypergraph with chromatic number $3$ there is a vertex contained in at least $(1+c)^r$ many edges? This was solved by Erdős and Lovász [ErLo75], who proved in particular that there is a vertex contained in at least $\frac{2^{r-1}}{4r}$ many edges.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

