@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/848.lean
@decl Erdos848.erdos_848
-- L4DEL: title: Is the maximum size of a set $A ⊆ \{1, \dots, N\}$ such that $ab + 1$ is never squarefree (for all $a, b ∈ A$) achieved by taking those $n ≡ 7 \pmod{25}$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is the maximum size of a set $A ⊆ \{1, \dots, N\}$ such that $ab + 1$ is never squarefree (for all $a, b ∈ A$) achieved by taking those $n ≡ 7 \pmod{25}$? This asks whether `Erdos848 N` holds for all $N$ (formulated using `A ⊆ Finset.range N`). This was solved for all sufficiently large $N$ by Sawhney in this note. In fact, Sawhney proves something slightly stronger, that there exists some constant $c>0$ such that if $\lvert A\rvert \geq (\frac{1}{25}-c)N$ and $N$ is large then $A$ is contained in either $\{ n\equiv 7\pmod{25}\}$ or $\{n\equiv 18\pmod{25}\}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/848.lean
@decl Erdos848.erdos_848.variants.asymptotic
-- L4DEL: title: There exists $N₀$ such that for all $N ≥ N₀$, if $A ⊆ \{1, \dots, N\}$ satisfies that $ab + 1$ is never squarefree for all $a, b ∈ A$, then $|A| ≤ |\{n ≤ N : n ≡ 7 \pmod{25}\}|$
-- L4DEL: intuition: There exists $N₀$ such that for all $N ≥ N₀$, if $A ⊆ \{1, \dots, N\}$ satisfies that $ab + 1$ is never squarefree for all $a, b ∈ A$, then $|A| ≤ |\{n ≤ N : n ≡ 7 \pmod{25}\}|$. More precisely, Sawhney proves: there exist absolute constants $η > 0$ and $N₀$ such that for all $N ≥ N₀$, if $|A| ≥ (1/25 - η)N$ then $A ⊆ \{n : n ≡ 7 \pmod{25}\}$ or $A ⊆ \{n : n ≡ 18 \pmod{25}\}$. A complete formal Lean 4 proof is available at: https://github.com/The-Obstacle-Is-The-Way/erdos-banger
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

