@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/87.lean
@decl Erdos87.erdos_87.parts.i
-- L4DEL: title: Let $0 < \epsilon < 1$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $0 < \epsilon < 1$. Is it true that, if $k$ is sufficiently large, then $$R(G) > (1-\epsilon)^k R(k)$$ for every graph $G$ with chromatic number $\chi(G)=k$? The restriction $\epsilon < 1$ excludes negative bases in $(1-\epsilon)^k$. This problem is #12 in Ramsey Theory in the graphs problem collection.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/87.lean
@decl Erdos87.erdos_87.parts.ii
