@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/881.lean
@decl Erdos881.IsMinimalAsymptoticAddBasisOfOrder
-- L4DEL: title: We interpret "additive basis of order `k`" as an asymptotic additive basis of order `k`, using the predicate `Set.IsAsymptoticAddBasisOfOrder` from additive combinatorics
-- L4DEL: intuition: We interpret "additive basis of order `k`" as an asymptotic additive basis of order `k`, using the predicate `Set.IsAsymptoticAddBasisOfOrder` from additive combinatorics. A *minimal* additive basis of order `k` is a set `A` such that * `A` is an asymptotic additive basis of order `k`, and * for every infinite subset `B ⊆ A`, the complement `A \ B` is *not* an asymptotic additive basis of order `k`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

