-- L4DEL: intuition: The set of all possible numbers of unit distances for a configuration of $n$ points.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/90.lean
@decl Erdos90.unitDistanceCounts_BddAbove
-- L4DEL: title: This lemma confirms that the set of possible unit distance counts is bounded above, which ensures that taking the supremum (`sSup`) is a well-defined operation
-- L4DEL: intuition: This lemma confirms that the set of possible unit distance counts is bounded above, which ensures that taking the supremum (`sSup`) is a well-defined operation. The trivial upper bound is the total number of pairs of points, $\binom{n}{2}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

