@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/914.lean
@decl Erdos914.erdos_914
-- L4DEL: title: Let $r\geq 2$ and $m\geq 1$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $r\geq 2$ and $m\geq 1$. Every graph with $rm$ vertices and minimum degree at least $m(r-1)$ contains $m$ vertex disjoint copies of $K_r$. When $r=2$ this follows from Dirac's theorem. Corrádi and Hajnal [CoHa63] proved this when $r=3$. Hajnal and Szemerédi [HaSz70] proved this for all $r\geq 4$. A shorter proof was given by Kierstead and Kostochka [KiKo08].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/914.lean
