-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: equitable_colouring
-- L4DEL: intuition: Equivalently, every graph with $rm$ vertices and maximum degree at most $m-1$ has a proper vertex colouring with $m$ colours in which every colour class has exactly $r$ vertices (an equitable colouring).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/915.lean
@decl Erdos915.erdos_915.variants.edge_disjoint
-- L4DEL: title: The edge-disjoint reading of erdős_915
-- L4DEL: intuition: The edge-disjoint reading of erdős_915. Mader [Ma73] proved that if a graph with $n$ vertices has more than $$\frac{m}{2}(n-1)-\frac{1}{2}(e_0(G)+\cdots+e_{m-2}(G))$$ edges then $G$ contains two vertices connected by $m$ edge-disjoint paths (where $e_r(G)$ counts the number of vertices of degree $\leq r$). In particular, this confirms (and is stronger than) the conjecture.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

