@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/939.lean
@decl Erdos939.Erdos939Sums
-- L4DEL: title: A set `S` belongs to `Erdos939Sums r` if it meets the following criteria: - The elements are positive
-- L4DEL: intuition: A set `S` belongs to `Erdos939Sums r` if it meets the following criteria: - The elements are positive. `0` has no prime factors, so it is vacuously `r`-powerful, and the source means positive integers. - The size of the set is `$|S| = r - 2$`. - The elements of the set are coprime (their greatest common divisor is 1). - Every element in `S` is an `$r$-powerful` number. - The sum of the elements in `S`, i.e., `$\sum_{s \in S} s$`, is also an `$r$-powerful` number. The summands are taken to be distinct (`S` is a `Finset`). The source does not say whether repeated summands are allowed; all known examples and constructions use distinct summands.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/939.lean
@decl Erdos939.erdos_939
-- L4DEL: title: If $r≥4$ then can the sum of $r-2$ coprime $r$-powerful numbers ever be itself $r$-powerful?
-- L4DEL: intuition: If $r≥4$ then can the sum of $r-2$ coprime $r$-powerful numbers ever be itself $r$-powerful?
