@decl Erdos940.erdos_940.variants.three_cubes
-- L4DEL: title: Is it true that the set of integers which are the sum of at most three cubes has density $0$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Is it true that the set of integers which are the sum of at most three cubes has density $0$? The cubes are those of non-negative integers, which is what `Multiset ℕ` gives. This choice decides the question: over `ℤ` a sum of three cubes is conjectured to represent every integer that is not $\pm 4 \bmod 9$, which is density $7/9$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

