@decl Erdos951.erdos_951.variants.beurling
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: beurling
-- L4DEL: intuition: Beurling conjectured that if `1 < a 0 < a 1 < ⋯` has property `Erdos951Prop` and the number of reals in $[1, x]$ of the form $\prod_i a_i^{k_i}$ is $x + o(\log x)$, then `a` must be the sequence of primes. Property `Erdos951Prop` makes distinct exponent vectors give distinct Beurling integers, so counting the set `BeurlingIntegers a` counts the generalised integers.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

