@decl Erdos965.erdos_965.variants.generalization
-- L4DEL: title: For every 2-coloring of ℝ, is there some $k ≥ 2$ and an uncountable set $A ⊆ ℝ$ such that all sums $a_1 + \cdots + a_k$ of $k$ distinct elements of $A$ have the same colour?
-- L4DEL: intuition: For every 2-coloring of ℝ, is there some $k ≥ 2$ and an uncountable set $A ⊆ ℝ$ such that all sums $a_1 + \cdots + a_k$ of $k$ distinct elements of $A$ have the same colour? In fact, in both [Ko16] and [SWCol] a single 2-coloring of ℝ is constructed such that for every $k ≥ 2$ and every uncountable $A ⊆ ℝ$ the sums of $k$ distinct elements of $A$ are not monochromatic.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

