@decl Erdos967.erdos_967.variants.tauberian
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: tauberian
-- L4DEL: intuition: Their interest in this problem arose from their proof that the statement that there are no such zeros is equivalent to the fact that, for any non-decreasing $f:\mathbb{R}\to \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ which is bounded on every bounded interval and is $=0$ for $x<1$, the relationship $$f(x)+\sum_k f(x/a_k)=\left(1+\sum_k \frac{1}{a_k}+o(1)\right)x$$ implies $f(x)=(1+o(1))x$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

