@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/990.lean
@decl Erdos990.erdos_990
-- L4DEL: title: Let $f=a_0+\cdots+a_dx^d\in \mathbb{C}[x]$ be a polynomial
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $f=a_0+\cdots+a_dx^d\in \mathbb{C}[x]$ be a polynomial. Is it true that, if $f$ has roots $z_1,\ldots,z_d$ with corresponding arguments $\theta_1,\ldots,\theta_d\in [0,2\pi]$, then for all intervals $I\subseteq [0,2\pi]$ $$ \left\lvert (\# \theta_i \in I) - \frac{\lvert I\rvert}{2\pi}d\right\rvert \ll \left(n\log M\right)^{1/2}, $$ where $n$ is the number of non-zero coefficients of $f$ and $$ M=\frac{\lvert a_0\rvert+\cdots +\lvert a_d\rvert}{(\lvert a_0\rvert\lvert a_d\rvert)^{1/2}}. $$ An internal OpenAI model (see [APSSV26b]) has disproved the conjecture, constructing, for every $n\geq 1$, a polynomial $f$ with $n$ non-zero coefficients such that $M<3$ and with a positive real zero of multiplicity $n-1$, whence letting $I=[0,c/d]$ for a suitably small $c>0$, $$ \left\lvert (\# \theta_i \in I) - \frac{\lvert I\rvert}{2\pi}d\right\rvert \geq n-1. $$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/990.lean
@decl Erdos990.erdos_990.variants.counterexample
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: counterexample
-- L4DEL: intuition: An internal OpenAI model (see [APSSV26b]) has disproved the conjecture, constructing, for every $n\geq 1$, a polynomial $f$ with $n$ non-zero coefficients such that $M<3$ and with a positive real zero of multiplicity $n-1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

