@decl Erdos995.erdos_995.variants.erdos_lower_bound
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: erdos_lower_bound
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős [Er49] showed the growth cannot be pushed below $N (\log\log N)^{1/2}$ by more than an arbitrarily small power: there is a lacunary sequence and a mean-zero $f \in L^2([0,1])$ such that for every $\varepsilon > 0$, for almost all $\alpha$, $$\limsup_{N \to \infty} \frac{\sum_{k < N} f(\{\alpha n_k\})}{N (\log\log N)^{1/2 - \varepsilon}} = \infty.$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

