-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $A$ be a set of $n$ positive integers. Does $A$ contain a sum-free set of size at least $\frac n 3 + Ω(n)$, where $Ω(n) → ∞$ as $n → ∞$? Bedert [Be25] proved that every set of $n$ integers contains a sum-free subset of size at least $\frac n 3 + c \log\log n$ for some absolute constant $c > 0$, so the answer is yes.
