@file FormalConjectures/GreensOpenProblems/18.lean
@decl Green18.green_18
-- L4DEL: title: Suppose that $G$ is a finite group, and let $A \subset G \times G$ be a subset of density $\alpha$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Suppose that $G$ is a finite group, and let $A \subset G \times G$ be a subset of density $\alpha$. Is it true that there are $\gg_\alpha |G|^3$ triples $x, y, g$ such that $(x, y), (gx, y), (x, gy)$ all lie in $A$? Note: A is taken as $\alpha$-dense, i.e. $|A| \ge \alpha |G|^2$ [Au16, Question 2]
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

