-- L4DEL: intuition: [So13] proved this is true for "BMZ corners". Follows from the proof of Theorem 2.1, p.1456-1457.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/GreensOpenProblems/18.lean
@decl Green18.numBmzCorners
-- L4DEL: title: The number of triples $(x, y, g)$ in $G^3$ such that $g \neq e$, and $(x, y), (xg, y), (x, gy)$ are all in $A$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The number of triples $(x, y, g)$ in $G^3$ such that $g \neq e$, and $(x, y), (xg, y), (x, gy)$ are all in $A$. These are called "BMZ corners" by [Au16].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

