@file FormalConjectures/GreensOpenProblems/19.lean
@decl Green19.green_19
-- L4DEL: title: What is $C$, the infimum of all exponents $c$ for which the following is true, uniformly for $0 < \alpha < 1$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: What is $C$, the infimum of all exponents $c$ for which the following is true, uniformly for $0 < \alpha < 1$? Suppose that $A \subset \mathbb{F}_2^n \times \mathbb{F}_2^n$ is a set of density $\alpha$. Write $N := 2^n$. Then there is some $d \neq 0$ such that $A$ contains $\gg \alpha^c N^2$ corners $(x,y), (x,y+d), (x+d,y)$. This question has been resolved by [FSS20], showing that $C = 4$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

