@decl Green31.IsGroupSidon
-- L4DEL: title: A subset $S$ of an abelian group is a Sidon set of the first kind in the sense of Babai and Sós [BS85] if $a + b = c + d$ with $a, b, c, d \in S$ implies $|\{a, b, c, d\}| \le 2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: A subset $S$ of an abelian group is a Sidon set of the first kind in the sense of Babai and Sós [BS85] if $a + b = c + d$ with $a, b, c, d \in S$ implies $|\{a, b, c, d\}| \le 2$. Unlike `IsSidon`, this allows $a + a = b + b$ with $a \ne b$.
