-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $p$ be a prime and let $A \subset \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$ be a set of size $\lfloor \sqrt{p} \rfloor$. Is there a dilate of $A$ containing a gap of length $100\sqrt{p}$?
