@file FormalConjectures/GreensOpenProblems/32.lean
@decl Green32.green_32.variants.dirichlet_regime
-- L4DEL: title: In the regime $\omega(p) \le c \log p$, this is basically Dirichlet's lower bound for the size of Bohr sets [Gr24]
-- L4DEL: intuition: In the regime $\omega(p) \le c \log p$, this is basically Dirichlet's lower bound for the size of Bohr sets [Gr24]. The lower bound $101 \le \omega(p)$ makes the set size $\lfloor \omega(p) \rfloor$ exceed $100$. With only $100 < \omega(p)$, a function with $100 < \omega(p) < 101$ asks for sets of size $100$ with a gap of length $p - 1$ in some dilate, which is impossible.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

