@decl Green36.green_36
-- L4DEL: title: Do the following exist, for arbitrarily large $n$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Do the following exist, for arbitrarily large $n$? An abelian group $H$ with $|H| = n^{2+o(1)}$, together with subsets $A_1, ..., A_n, B_1, ..., B_n$ satisfying $|A_i||B_i| \ge n^{2-o(1)}$ and $|A_i + B_i| = |A_i||B_i|$, such that the sets $A_i + B_i$ are disjoint from the sets $A_j + B_k$ ($j \neq k$)? NOTE: according to [CKS05, 4.1], the conditions should be $A_i + B_j$ disjoint from $A_j + B_k$ for $i \neq k$. See `green_36.variants.cks05`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

