-- L4DEL: intuition: Defines a family of subsets of $A_n$ where each permutation $\pi$ in a subset obeys $\pi(x)$ and $\forall v \in I$, $\pi(v)\notin I$ for a fixed $x$ and $I$. It is easy to demonstrate that such a subset is product-free, because for any a,b,c in such a set, $(a*b) (x)=a(b(x))\notin I$ but $c(x) in I$
