-- L4DEL: intuition: Definition 2.1 from [CoEl03]: A function is admissible if it is continuous and both the function and its Fourier transform decay sufficiently fast. Continuity is essential: changing `f` at a single point leaves `fHat f` unchanged, so without it every positive bound would be achievable.
