-- L4DEL: intuition: The real-valued Fourier transform used in the Cohn--Elkies conditions. For real radial admissible functions, the complex Fourier transform is expected to be real-valued; we take `.re` to expose the real scalar used in the inequality. **Convention:** Mathlib's `𝓕 f w` expands to $\int e^{-2\pi i \langle v, w \rangle} f(v) dv$, which matches [CoEl03]'s $\hat{f}(t) = \int f(x) e^{-2\pi i \langle x, t \rangle} dx$.
