@file FormalConjectures/HilbertProblems/5.lean
@decl Hilbert5.hilbert_smith_conjecture.variants.riemannian
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: riemannian
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Hilbert–Smith conjecture holds for actions by isometries of a connected smooth Riemannian manifold `X`: the isometry group of `X` is a Lie group by the Myers–Steenrod theorem, so `G` has no small subgroups and is a Lie group by the Gleason–Montgomery–Zippin theorem. Here `X` carries its Riemannian distance (`IsRiemannianManifold`), so the metric topology of `X` is its manifold topology.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

