@file FormalConjectures/Kourovka/1_74.lean
@decl Kourovka.«1.74».kourovka_1_74.variants.tarski_monster
-- L4DEL: title: There exists a Tarski monster group that admits a non-discrete Hausdorff group topology
-- L4DEL: intuition: There exists a Tarski monster group that admits a non-discrete Hausdorff group topology. This follows from Theorem 1.4 of Klyachko, Olshanskii and Osin, which gives a topologizable Tarski monster of every sufficiently large odd exponent $n$; taking $n$ to be a prime $p$ makes every non-trivial proper subgroup cyclic of order $p$. Any such group is a minimal topological group.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

