-- L4DEL: intuition: Basic conditions on initial velocity field for the Navier-Stokes equations in $n$-dimensional space. The initial velocity must be: - Divergence-free (incompressibility condition: $\nabla \cdot u_0 = 0$) - Smooth ($C^\infty$) These conditions apply regardless of spatial dimension.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Millennium/NavierStokes.lean
@decl NavierStokes.InitialVelocityConditionDecay
-- L4DEL: title: Initial velocity conditions for the Navier-Stokes problem on all of $\mathbb{R}^n$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Initial velocity conditions for the Navier-Stokes problem on all of $\mathbb{R}^n$. In addition to being smooth and divergence-free, the velocity must decay faster than any polynomial at spatial infinity (condition 4 in Fefferman's paper). This condition ensures the velocity field has finite energy and reasonable behavior as $\lVert x \rVert \to \infty$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

