@file FormalConjectures/Millennium/NavierStokes.lean
@decl NavierStokes.IsOnePeriodic
-- L4DEL: title: A function $f : \mathbb{R}^n \to \alpha$ is 1-periodic if it is periodic in each coordinate with period $1$, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: A function $f : \mathbb{R}^n \to \alpha$ is 1-periodic if it is periodic in each coordinate with period $1$, i.e. $f(x + e_i) = f(x)$ for each unit vector $e_i$. This captures functions on the $n$-torus $\mathbb{R}^n/\mathbb{Z}^n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

