@file FormalConjectures/Millennium/NavierStokes.lean
@decl NavierStokes.NavierStokesExistenceAndSmoothness
-- L4DEL: title: A solution (v, p) to the Navier-Stokes equations in n-dimensional space with viscosity $\nu$, initial velocity $u_0$, and external force $f$
-- L4DEL: intuition: A solution (v, p) to the Navier-Stokes equations in n-dimensional space with viscosity $\nu$, initial velocity $u_0$, and external force $f$. This structure captures the core requirements for a solution: 1. The velocity and pressure satisfy the Navier-Stokes PDE (equation 1) 2. The velocity remains divergence-free for all time (equation 2) 3. The initial condition is satisfied (equation 3) 4. The solution is smooth ($C^\infty$) for all time $t \ge 0$ (equations 6, 11)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

