@file FormalConjectures/Millennium/RiemannHypothesis.lean
@decl GRH.trivialZeros
-- L4DEL: title: Let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character, `trivialZeros` is the set of trivial zeros of the Dirichlet $L$-function of $\chi$ which is always a set of non-positive integers
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $\chi$ be a Dirichlet character, `trivialZeros` is the set of trivial zeros of the Dirichlet $L$-function of $\chi$ which is always a set of non-positive integers. - $\chi = 1$ then the Dirichlet $L$-function is the Riemann zeta function, having trivial zeroes at all negative even integers (exclude $0$). - $\chi$ is odd, then the trivial zeroes are the negative odd integers. - $\chi \neq 1$ is even, then the trivial zeroes are the non-positive even integers.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

