-- L4DEL: title: The primary defining sequence `a`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The primary defining sequence `a`. Pentanacci $\pi$ sequence: $a(1)=a(2)=a(3)=a(4)=a(5)=1$; for $n>5$, $a(n) = \pi(\sum_{j=1}^5 a(n-j))$ where $\pi = A000720$. Note on indices: for $n \ge 0$, $a(n)$ corresponds to $A_{n+1}$ in the OEIS sequence.
