@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/103662.lean
@decl OeisA103662.a
-- L4DEL: title: The primary defining sequence `a`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The primary defining sequence `a`. `a n` is the smallest power with base $>1$ and exponent $n$ whose decimal representation doesn't contain the digit 0. $$a(n) = (\min \{ b \in \mathbb{N} \mid b > 1, \text{decimal representation of } b^n \text{ contains no digit } 0 \})^n$$ If no such base exists, `sInf` of an empty set of naturals returns 0, so `a n = 0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

