@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/105020.lean
@decl OeisA105020.a
-- L4DEL: title: The primary defining sequence `a`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The primary defining sequence `a`. Array read by upward antidiagonals: row $n$ ($n \ge 0$) contains the numbers $m^2 - n^2$, $m \ge n+1$. The array entry $T(i, j)$ is $(i+j+1)^2 - i^2$. The sequence $a(n)$ is generated by reading $T(i, j)$ for $i+j=c$, with $i$ decreasing from $c$ to $0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

