-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: "It is conjectured that $\binom{6n-2}{2n} / \left(2 \binom{4n-1}{2n}\right) = \text{A005156}(n+1)/\text{A005156}(n)$." The OEIS comment indexes A005156 from $1$; for the $0$-indexed sequence `b` this states `frac (n + 1) = b (n + 1) / b n`. This holds by the product formula $$\text{A005156}(n) = \frac{1}{2^n} \prod_{k=1}^{n} \frac{(6k-2)!\,(2k-1)!}{(4k-1)!\,(4k-2)!}$$ conjectured by Robbins and proved by Kuperberg (2002).
