-- L4DEL: intuition: Second part of the conjecture, $a(2^n)=\textrm{A033638}(n)=\lfloor n^2 / 4 \rfloor + 1$. It holds by induction on $n$, since $a(2^{n+1}) = a(2^n) + a(2^n - 2)$ for $n \ge 1$ and $a(2^m - 2) = \lfloor (m+1)/2 \rfloor$ for $m \ge 1$.
