@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/11545.lean
@decl OeisA11545.conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture2
-- L4DEL: intuition: Number of collisions occurring in a system consisting of an infinitely massive, rigid wall at the origin, a ball with mass m stationary at position $x_1 > 0$, and a ball with mass $(10^2n)m$ at position $x_2 > x_1$ and rolling toward the origin, assuming perfectly elastic collisions and no friction. Strictly speaking, this property, which is equivalent to the statement that the interval $(m\pi, \pi/\textrm{arctan}(1/m))$ does not contain an integer for all $m = 10^n$, is not known to be true for sure. In other words, we do not know for certain that A332045 does not contain a power of $10$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

