@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/153330.lean
@decl OeisA153330.conjecture3
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 3 (Ya-Ping Lu, 2024): Except 1, 3 and 6, the absolute value of all terms can be written as $5x + 8y$ for $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture 3 (Ya-Ping Lu, 2024): Except 1, 3 and 6, the absolute value of all terms can be written as $5x + 8y$ for $x, y \in \mathbb{N}$. (Note: in the OEIS comment, "x and y are integers" means $x$ and $y$ have the same sign, i.e., $|v| = 5x + 8y$ with $x, y \ge 0$, since every integer is a $\mathbb{Z}$-linear combination of 5 and 8).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

