@decl OeisA157237.conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: On Feb
-- L4DEL: intuition: On Feb. 24, 2009, Zhi-Wei Sun conjectured that $a(n) = 0$ if and only if $n < 16$ or $n \in \{18, 21, 24, 51, 84, 1011, 59586\}$; in other words, except for $35, 41, 47, 101, 167, 2021, 119171$, any odd integer greater than $30$ can be written as the sum of a prime congruent to $1 \bmod 6$, a positive power of $2$ and eleven times a positive power of $2$.
