@decl OeisA160324.conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture2
-- L4DEL: intuition: For each integer $m > 2$, any natural number $n$ can be written in the form $p_{m+1}(x_1) + \cdots + p_{2m}(x_m)$ with $x_1, \dots, x_m$ nonnegative integers, where $p_k(x) = (k-2)x(x-1)/2 + x$ ($x=0,1,2,\dots$) are $k$-gonal numbers. - _Zhi-Wei Sun_, Aug 15 2009
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

