@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/1818.lean
@decl OeisA1818.conjecture1
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture1
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture 1: For any primitive $2n$-th root $\zeta$ of unity, the permanent of the $2n \times 2n$ matrix $[m(j,k)]_{j,k=1..2n}$ coincides with $a(n) = ((2n-1)!!)^2$, where $m(j,k)$ is $(1+\zeta^{j-k})/(1-\zeta^{j-k})$ if $j \neq k$, and $1$ otherwise. - Zhi-Wei Sun, Dec 21 2021
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/1818.lean
@decl OeisA1818.conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 2: Let $p$ be an odd prime
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture 2: Let $p$ be an odd prime. Then the permanent of the $(p-1) \times (p-1)$ matrix $[f(j,k)]_{j,k=1..p-1}$ is congruent to $a((p-1)/2) = ((p-2)!!)^2 \pmod{p^2}$, where $f(j,k)$ is $(j+k)/(j-k)$ if $j \neq k$, and $f(j,k) = 1$ otherwise. - Zhi-Wei Sun, Dec 22 2021
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

