@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/24356.lean
@decl OeisA24356.conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: "I conjecture that $a(4)$ is the only zero
-- L4DEL: intuition: "I conjecture that $a(4)$ is the only zero. - _Jon Perry_, Mar 22 2004" Stated as a biconditional: the claim that $a(4)$ is *the only* zero asserts both that $a(4) = 0$ and that no other index vanishes. A bare implication `a n = 0 → n = 4` would be satisfied vacuously by a sequence with no zero at all. The existence direction is certified by `a_4`; the uniqueness direction is the open part.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

