@decl OeisA267581.a
-- L4DEL: title: Decimal representation of the middle column of the "Rule 167" elementary cellular automaton starting with a single ON (black) cell
-- L4DEL: intuition: Decimal representation of the middle column of the "Rule 167" elementary cellular automaton starting with a single ON (black) cell. The term $a(n)$ is the decimal value of the binary number $C_{0, 0} C_{1, 0} \dots C_{n, 0}$, where $C_{i, 0}$ is the state of the center cell at time $i$. $$a(n) = \sum_{k=0}^n C_{k, 0} \cdot 2^{n-k}$$
