@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/278070.lean
@decl OeisA278070.a
-- L4DEL: title: a: $a(n) = \text{hypergeometric}([n, -n], [], -1)$
-- L4DEL: intuition: a: $a(n) = \text{hypergeometric}([n, -n], [], -1)$. This is equivalent to the combinatorial sum: $$a(n) = \sum_{k=0}^n \binom{n}{k} \binom{n+k-1}{k} k!$$ The expression uses $\mathbb{N}$ arithmetic throughout, safely handling the subtraction via `Nat.pred`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

