@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/323557.lean
@decl OeisA323557.a
-- L4DEL: title: Coefficients of G.f
-- L4DEL: intuition: Coefficients of G.f. $\sum_{n\ge 0} x^n \cdot \frac{(1 + x^n)^n}{(1 + x^{n+1})^{n+1}}$. The $m$-th term $a(m)$ is the coefficient of $x^m$, which is explicitly given by the sum: $$ a(m) = \sum_{n=0}^m \sum_{k=0}^n \binom{n}{k} (-1)^j \binom{n+j}{j},$$ where $j = \frac{m - n(k+1)}{n+1}$, and the term is zero unless $j$ is a natural number.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/325046.lean
@decl OeisA325046.a
-- L4DEL: title: Coefficients of G.f
-- L4DEL: intuition: Coefficients of G.f. $\sum_{n \ge 0} x^n \cdot \frac{(1 + x^n)^n}{(1 - x^{n+1})^{n+1}}$. The term $a(N)$ is the coefficient of $x^N$ in the generating function. Expanding the terms, we get a formula for $a(N)$: $$a(N) = \sum_{n=0}^N \sum_{k=0}^n \mathbf{1}_{n + nk + (n+1)j = N} \binom{n}{k} \binom{n+j}{j}$$ where $j = \frac{N - n(k+1)}{n+1}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/340737.lean
@decl OeisA340737.a
-- L4DEL: title: Numerators of a sequence of fractions converging to $e$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Numerators of a sequence of fractions converging to $e$. $$a(1) = 3, a(2) = 5$$ For $n > 2$: $$a(n) = \begin{cases} \left(\frac{n+2}{2}\right) a(n-1) - a(n-2) - \left(\frac{n-2}{2}\right) a(n-3) & \text{if } n \text{ is even} \cr 2 a(n-1) + n a(n-2) & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \end{cases}$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/340737.lean
@decl OeisA340737.b
-- L4DEL: title: Denominators of a sequence of fractions converging to $e$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Denominators of a sequence of fractions converging to $e$. This sequence is defined by the same recurrence relation as a but with initial values $b(1)=1, b(2)=2$. $$b(1) = 1, b(2) = 2$$ For $n > 2$: $$b(n) = \begin{cases} \left(\frac{n+2}{2}\right) b(n-1) - b(n-2) - \left(\frac{n-2}{2}\right) b(n-3) & \text{if } n \text{ is even} \cr 2 b(n-1) + n b(n-2) & \text{if } n \text{ is odd} \end{cases}$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

