@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/358684.lean
@decl OeisA358684.oeis_358684_conjecture_0
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture: the dyadic valuation of A93179(n) - 1 does not exceed 2^n - a(n)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture: the dyadic valuation of A93179(n) - 1 does not exceed 2^n - a(n). A93179(n) is minFac(fermatNumber n), the smallest prime factor of the n-th Fermat number. The conjecture states that if $P_n$ is the smallest prime factor of the $n$-th Fermat number, then $\nu_2(P_n - 1) \le 2^n - a(n)$. Substituting the definition of $a(n)$, this is equivalent to $\nu_2(P_n - 1) \le \lfloor \log_2(P_n) \rfloor$. This is Conjecture 3.4 in [SA22].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

