-- L4DEL: intuition: $a(n)$ is the smallest composite number $c$ such that $\textrm{primorial}(n) + c$ is prime.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/38771.lean
@decl OeisA38771.a_n_exists
-- L4DEL: title: $a(n) \ne 0$ for all $n$ (i.e., a suitable composite $c$ always exists)
-- L4DEL: intuition: $a(n) \ne 0$ for all $n$ (i.e., a suitable composite $c$ always exists). The following more general statement follows from Dirichlet's theorem on primes in arithmetic progressions: there doesn't exist a > 0 natural number such that p - a is prime for every prime p > a. Choose q prime such that q is coprime with a, and p > a + q prime such that q | p - a (such a p exists from Dirichlet's theorem). Then p - a is composite, a contradiction.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/38771.lean
@decl OeisA38771.conjecture1
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture: $\liminf_{n \to \infty} \frac{a(n)}{p_{n+1}^2} = 1 <$ $\limsup_{n \to \infty} \frac{a(n)}{p_{n+1}^2} = 2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture: $\liminf_{n \to \infty} \frac{a(n)}{p_{n+1}^2} = 1 <$ $\limsup_{n \to \infty} \frac{a(n)}{p_{n+1}^2} = 2$. - Charles R Greathouse IV and Thomas Ordowski, Apr 24 2015
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/38771.lean
@decl OeisA38771.conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: All the terms in this sequence have exactly two prime factors
-- L4DEL: intuition: All the terms in this sequence have exactly two prime factors. This conjecture is true for the first 133 terms. - Dmitry Kamenetsky, Jan 06 2019
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

