-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture I: if $n > 2$, then $\frac{a(\text{A005382}(n))}{12}$ is prime, where A005382 is the sequence of primes $p$ such that $2p-1$ is also prime
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture I: if $n > 2$, then $\frac{a(\text{A005382}(n))}{12}$ is prime, where A005382 is the sequence of primes $p$ such that $2p-1$ is also prime. Since $\text{A005382}(1) = 2$, $\text{A005382}(2) = 3$ and $\text{A005382}(3) = 7$, this says that $\frac{a(p)}{12}$ is prime for every prime $p > 3$ such that $2p-1$ is also prime. - Lorenzo Sauras Altuzarra, Oct 13 2020
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

