@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/60841.lean
@decl OeisA60841.conjecture2
-- L4DEL: title: "All denominators are powers of two (A000079)." - _Robert G
-- L4DEL: intuition: "All denominators are powers of two (A000079)." - _Robert G. Wilson v_, Aug 02 2015 This is false: for $n = 1807$ the denominator of $1/\det(M)$ is divisible by $3$. See T. Adamczewski, OEIS Open: How many conjectures can language models turn into theorems?, arXiv:2608.11941. The Lean disproof there uses the closed form $1/\det(M) = \prod_{k=1}^n k^2/\varphi(k)$ from the OEIS entry: https://github.com/epoch-research/LeanOpenProblems-results/blob/fd09021e79869476ef83cda231312f1a2a89c8d7/runs/oeis-full-50usd-ant-j0j0g4uzligm1k41/oeis_60841_conjecture_0/Submission/Spec.lean#L272
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

