@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/69922.lean
@decl OeisA69922.conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Question: for any $n > 0$, is there at least one prime $p$ such that $n^n \le p \le n^n + n^2$?
-- L4DEL: intuition: Question: for any $n > 0$, is there at least one prime $p$ such that $n^n \le p \le n^n + n^2$? In this case, that would be stronger than the Schinzel conjecture: "for $m > 1$ there's at least one prime $p$ such that $m \le p \le m + \log(m)^2$" since $n^2 < \log(n^n)^2 = n^2 \log(n)^2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

