@decl OeisA87455.SatisfiesBenford
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: SatisfiesBenford
-- L4DEL: intuition: A sequence of integers satisfies Benford's law if, for every $t \in [1, 10)$, the asymptotic relative frequency of terms whose decimal significand is at most $t$ equals $\log_{10} t$ (Berger-Hill). This is strictly stronger than the law for the leading digit alone.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

