@file FormalConjectures/OEIS/945.lean
@decl OeisA945.every_prime_occurs
-- L4DEL: title: "Does the sequence
-- L4DEL: intuition: "Does the sequence ... contain every prime? ... [It] was considered by Guy and Nowakowski and later by Shanks, [Wagstaff93] computed the sequence through the 43rd term. The computational problem inherent in continuing the sequence further is the enormous size of the numbers that must be factored. Already the number $a(1) \cdots a(43) + 1$ has 180 digits." - [CrandallPomerance01] See also [Mullin63].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

