@decl OeisA96535.conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: All numbers appear infinitely often, i.e., for every number $k \ge 0$ and every frequency $f > 0$ there is an index $i$ such that $a(i) = k$ is the $f$-th occurrence of $k$ in the sequence. - _Klaus Brockhaus_, Aug 29 2006
