@file FormalConjectures/OpenQuantumProblems/35.lean
@decl OpenQuantumProblem35.ame_7_exists_iff
-- L4DEL: title: For a physical local dimension $d \ge 2$, a seven-party AME state exists exactly when $d \ge 3$
-- L4DEL: intuition: For a physical local dimension $d \ge 2$, a seven-party AME state exists exactly when $d \ge 3$. The hypothesis excludes the degenerate dimension $d = 1$, for which the unique computational-basis state is AME under the definitions of this file. Shi--Zhang--Zhao--Li (2026) construct cyclic quadratic-phase states in every odd dimension and a coupled binary--odd-dimensional state in every dimension congruent to `2` modulo `4`; together with power-of-two constructions and the product property, this covers every `d ≥ 3`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

