@file FormalConjectures/OptimizationConstants/1a.lean
@decl Constant1a.C1a
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: C1a
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Tao's Optimization constant 1a / An autocorrelation constant related to Sidon sets**: The largest constant $C$ such that $$\max_{-1/2 \le t \le 1/2} \int_{\mathbb{R}} f(t - x) f(x)\,dx \ge C \left(\int_{-1/4}^{1/4} f(x)\,dx\right)^2$$ for all nonnegative $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$. The inequality is only required for square-integrable $f$. This does not change the constant (see [M2010, §2]), and it guarantees that every autoconvolution integral exists and that the supremum over $t$ is finite. This number is related to the maximal size of Sidon sets in additive combinatorics.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

