@file FormalConjectures/Other/SuffixPrefixAvoidance.lean
@decl SuffixPrefixAvoidance.suffix_prefix_avoidance_bound
-- L4DEL: title: $A$ and $B$ are sets of words of length $n$ over alphabet with $q \geq 1$ letters
-- L4DEL: intuition: $A$ and $B$ are sets of words of length $n$ over alphabet with $q \geq 1$ letters. No suffix of a word in $A$ coincides with a prefix of a word in $B$. Then $|A| \cdot |B|$ is at most $\frac{q^{2n}}{en}$. This problem is from *Maximal sets of strings with no prefix-suffix overlap* and was proved in *An isoperimetric inequality for word overlap*.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

