-- L4DEL: title: $K^M_n(\mathbb{C}(x_1, \dots, x_m))/p = 0$ for $n > m$: the field has cohomological dimension $m$ [Serre1997, Ch
-- L4DEL: intuition: $K^M_n(\mathbb{C}(x_1, \dots, x_m))/p = 0$ for $n > m$: the field has cohomological dimension $m$ [Serre1997, Ch. II, §4.2], so $H^n(\mathbb{C}(x_1, \dots, x_m), \mu_p^{\otimes n}) = 0$, and $K^M_n/p \cong H^n(-, \mu_p^{\otimes n})$ by the norm residue isomorphism theorem [Voevodsky2011].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

