@file FormalConjectures/Paper/BranchingVAS.lean
@decl BranchingVAS.reachability_decidable
-- L4DEL: title: The reachability problem for branching vector addition systems is decidable
-- L4DEL: intuition: The reachability problem for branching vector addition systems is decidable. That is, the predicate taking a dimension `d`, a branching vector addition system `b` of dimension `d` and a target vector `t ∈ ℤ^d`, and returning whether `t` is reachable in `b`, is a computable predicate. Note that the dimension is part of the input: a single algorithm must work for all dimensions. As of August 2026, the solution is quite recently announced and is not yet peer-reviewed.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

