@decl KaplanskyUInvariant.isGreatest_anisotropicDims_complex
-- L4DEL: title: $u(\mathbb{C}) = 1$ [MerkurjevParimala2025, §5.1]: the form $x^2$ is anisotropic, and every quadratic form in two or more variables over an algebraically closed field is isotropic
-- L4DEL: intuition: $u(\mathbb{C}) = 1$ [MerkurjevParimala2025, §5.1]: the form $x^2$ is anisotropic, and every quadratic form in two or more variables over an algebraically closed field is isotropic.
