@file FormalConjectures/Paper/KotzigConjecture.lean
@decl KotzigConjecture.kotzig_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: For any tree $T$ with $n$ edges, the complete graph $K_{2n+1}$ decomposes into $2n+1$ edge-disjoint copies of $T$ via cyclic shifts of a single embedding
-- L4DEL: intuition: For any tree $T$ with $n$ edges, the complete graph $K_{2n+1}$ decomposes into $2n+1$ edge-disjoint copies of $T$ via cyclic shifts of a single embedding. The $2n+1$ copies are $f_0, f_1, \dots, f_{2n}$ where $f_i(v) = f_0(v) + i$ for all vertices $v$ — each copy is obtained by adding $i \pmod{2n+1}$ to every vertex of the base copy. This is strictly stronger than `RingelConjecture.ringel_conjecture`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

