@file FormalConjectures/Paper/LatinSquare.lean
@decl LatinSquare.growthRateZn
-- L4DEL: title: Conjecture 6.9 in [Wa2011]: $$ \lim_{\substack{n \to \infty \\ n \text{ odd}}} \frac{1}{n} \log(z_n / n!) = -1 $$ It is not even known if this limit exists
-- L4DEL: intuition: Conjecture 6.9 in [Wa2011]: $$ \lim_{\substack{n \to \infty \\ n \text{ odd}}} \frac{1}{n} \log(z_n / n!) = -1 $$ It is not even known if this limit exists. Note that $z_n = 0$ for even $n$ (see `z_even`), so the limit must be restricted to odd $n$; here we parametrise odd $n$ as $2k + 1$.
