@file FormalConjectures/Paper/PrimeTuples.lean
@decl PrimeTuplesConjecture.prime_tuples_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: For any `k ≥ 2`, let `a₁,...,aₖ` and `b₁,...,bₖ` be integers with `aᵢ > 0`
-- L4DEL: intuition: For any `k ≥ 2`, let `a₁,...,aₖ` and `b₁,...,bₖ` be integers with `aᵢ > 0`. Suppose that for every prime `p` there exists an integer `n` such that `p ∤ ∏ i, (aᵢ n + bᵢ)`. Then there exist infinitely many `n` such that `aᵢ n + bᵢ` is prime for all `i`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

