@file FormalConjectures/Paper/ReedOmegaDeltaChi.lean
@decl ReedOmegaDeltaChi.reed_omega_delta_chi_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: For a graph $G$, we define $\Delta(G)$ to be the maximum degree, $\omega(G)$ to be the size of the largest clique subgraph, and $\chi(G)$ to be the chromatic number
-- L4DEL: intuition: For a graph $G$, we define $\Delta(G)$ to be the maximum degree, $\omega(G)$ to be the size of the largest clique subgraph, and $\chi(G)$ to be the chromatic number. Reed's omega, delta, and chi conjecture states that $$\chi(G) \leq \lceil \frac{1}{2}(\omega(G) + \Delta(G) + 1) \rceil.$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

