@decl RiemannHypothesis.IsTestFunction
-- L4DEL: title: The additive condition on test functions
-- L4DEL: intuition: The additive condition on test functions. The property in [Co26] that $\hat{g}(\pm i/2) = 0$, where $\hat{g}$ is the Mellin transform, corresponds to the vanishing of the Fourier transform at $\pm 1/2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Paper/RiemannHypothesisEquivalents.lean
@decl RiemannHypothesis.lagarias_criterion
-- L4DEL: title: Lagarias' Criterion**
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Lagarias' Criterion**. A refinement of Robin's criterion: the Riemann Hypothesis is equivalent to $$ \sigma(n) < H_n + e^{H_n}\log H_n $$ for all $n \geq 2$, where $H_n = 1 + 1/2 + \cdots + 1/n$ is the $n$th harmonic number. Note that [Co26] states this for all $n \geq 1$, but at $n = 1$ both sides equal $1$; Lagarias' original formulation is the non-strict inequality for all $n \geq 1$, with equality only at $n = 1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Paper/RiemannHypothesisEquivalents.lean
@decl RiemannHypothesis.lagarias_criterion_rhs
