@file FormalConjectures/Paper/RiemannHypothesisEquivalents.lean
@decl RiemannHypothesis.lambda
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: lambda
-- L4DEL: intuition: The numbers $$ \lambda_n := \sum_{\rho}\left(1 - \left(1 - \frac{1}{\rho}\right)^n\right) $$ appearing in Li's criterion, summing over the nontrivial zeros $\rho$ of the Riemann zeta function. This is a real number because nontrivial zeros always come in conjugate pairs. Note that, as stated, the sum is only conditionally convergent, however it is absolutely convergent when taken in conjugate pairs, since $1/\rho + 1/\bar\rho = 2\Re\rho/|\rho|^2$. Hence we sum over the zeros with positive imaginary part with summand `2 * (_).re`, which makes the unordered sum `∑'` meaningful.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Paper/RiemannHypothesisEquivalents.lean
@decl RiemannHypothesis.li_criterion
-- L4DEL: title: Li's Criterion**
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Li's Criterion**. The Riemann Hypothesis is equivalent to the positivity of $$ \lambda_n := \sum_{\rho}\left(1 - \left(1 - \frac{1}{\rho}\right)^n\right) $$ for each $n > 0$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

