@decl RiemannZetaMoments.arithmeticFactor
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: arithmeticFactor
-- L4DEL: intuition: The arithmetic factor expected to appear in the asymptotic behaviour of the $k$th moment of the Riemann zeta function, defined by $$ a_k = \prod_{p \text{ prime}} (1 - 1/p)^{k^2} \sum_{m=0}^{\infty} \binom{m+k-1}{m}^2 p^{-m}. $$ For $k \ge 1$ we have $\binom{m+k-1}{m} = \Gamma(m+k)/(m!\,\Gamma(k))$. We use `Nat.multichoose`, so that $a_0 = 1$ and the Keating–Snaith formula also holds for $k = 0$.
