@file FormalConjectures/Paper/SerreUniformity.lean
@decl SerreUniformity.serre_uniformity.variants.bound_37
-- L4DEL: title: Serre's uniformity conjecture over $\mathbb{Q}$, explicit form**: the bound $C = 37$ works, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Serre's uniformity conjecture over $\mathbb{Q}$, explicit form**: the bound $C = 37$ works, i.e. every non-CM elliptic curve over $\mathbb{Q}$ has surjective mod-$p$ Galois representation for every prime $p > 37$. From the introduction of [Lem17]: "This conjecture remains open today, but, over the last forty years, there has been a lot of progress towards a proof for $K = \mathbb{Q}$ — it is believed that, in this case, $p_K = 37$."
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

