@file FormalConjectures/Paper/StrongSensitivityConjecture.lean
@decl StrongSensitivityConjecture.nisanExample
-- L4DEL: title: Simple test example
-- L4DEL: intuition: Simple test example. For multiples of four with $n \ge 12$, this Boolean function has block sensitivity strictly greater than its sensitivity. Source: Nisan1989. `nisanExample(x) = 1` iff the Hamming weight of $x$ is either $n/2$ or $n/2 + 1$. The function is symmetric, so its value only depends on the Hamming weight of the input.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Paper/StrongSensitivityConjecture.lean
@decl StrongSensitivityConjecture.nisanExample_blockSensitivity
-- L4DEL: title: Assuming `n` is a multiple of 4 and $n \ge 8$, the block sensitivity of `nisanExample` is $3n/4$, achieved by any $x$ with Hamming weight $n/2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Assuming `n` is a multiple of 4 and $n \ge 8$, the block sensitivity of `nisanExample` is $3n/4$, achieved by any $x$ with Hamming weight $n/2$. An optimal block configuration uses all $n/2$ one-bits as singleton blocks and forms $n/4$ disjoint size-2 blocks from the zero-bits.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Paper/StrongSensitivityConjecture.lean
@decl StrongSensitivityConjecture.nisanExample_sensitivity
-- L4DEL: title: Assuming `n` is a positive multiple of 4, the sensitivity of `nisanExample` is $n/2 + 2$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Assuming `n` is a positive multiple of 4, the sensitivity of `nisanExample` is $n/2 + 2$. It is achieved by any $x$ with Hamming weight $n/2 + 2$: flipping any of its $n/2 + 2$ one-bits moves the input into the accepting layer of weight $n/2 + 1$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

