@file FormalConjectures/Paper/TuDengConjecture.lean
@decl TuDengConjecture.tu_deng_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: tu_deng_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **The Tu-Deng conjecture.** For $k \ge 2$ and a nonzero residue $t$ modulo $2^k - 1$, there are at most $2^{k-1}$ pairs of residues $(a, b)$ with $a + b = t$ whose binary weights (of their representatives in $0, \dots, 2^k - 2$) sum to at most $k - 1$. Proved in [LLX26] and independently in [Cu26]; see also the Lean development [Lean26].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

