@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/BatemanHornConjecture.lean
@decl BatemanHornConjecture.bateman_horn_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: bateman_horn_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **The Bateman-Horn Conjecture** Given a finite collection of distinct irreducible polynomials non-constant $f_1, f_2, \dots, f_k \in \mathbb{Z}[x]$ with positive leading coefficients that satisfy the Schinzel condition, the number of positive integers $n \leq x$ for which all polynomials $f_i$ are simultaneously prime is asymptotic to: $$\frac{C}{D} \frac{x}{(\log x)^k}$$ where $D = \prod_i \deg(f_i)$ and $C$ is the Bateman-Horn constant given by the convergent infinite product: $$C = \prod_{p\in\mathbb{P}} (1 - 1/p)^{-k} (1 - \omega_p/p)$$ Here $\omega_p$ is the number of residue classes modulo $p$ for which at least one polynomial vanishes. The product is only conditionally convergent: it is the limit as $N \to \infty$ of the partial products over the primes $p < N$. The Schinzel condition ensures that for each prime $p$, there exists some integer $n$ such that $p$ does not divide the product $f_1(n) f_2(n) \dotsb f_k(n)$, which guarantees the infinite product converges to a positive value.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/BatemanHornConjecture.lean
@decl BatemanHornConjecture.BatemanHornPartialProduct
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: BatemanHornPartialProduct
-- L4DEL: intuition: The partial Euler product of the Bateman-Horn constant of a set of polynomials `S`, taken over the primes $p < N$: $$\prod_{p < N} (1 - \frac{1}{p})^{-|S|} (1 - \frac{\omega_p(S)}{p})$$ where $\omega_p(S)$ is the number of residue classes mod $p$ where at least one polynomial in $S$ vanishes. The Bateman-Horn constant is the limit of these partial products as $N \to \infty$; the product is only conditionally convergent, so the order of the factors matters.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/BatemanHornConjecture.lean
@decl BatemanHornConjecture.CountSimultaneousPrimes
-- L4DEL: title: `CountSimultaneousPrimes S x` counts the number of `n ≤ x` at which all polynomials in `S` attain a prime value
-- L4DEL: intuition: `CountSimultaneousPrimes S x` counts the number of `n ≤ x` at which all polynomials in `S` attain a prime value.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

