@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/BetrothedNumbers.lean
@decl BetrothedNumbers.same_parity_betrothed
-- L4DEL: title: Same parity betrothed numbers conjecture.** Do there exist betrothed numbers $(m, n)$ where both have the same parity (both even or both odd)?
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Same parity betrothed numbers conjecture.** Do there exist betrothed numbers $(m, n)$ where both have the same parity (both even or both odd)? All known betrothed pairs consist of one even and one odd number. The requirement $m \neq n$ is part of the question: $\mathrm{IsBetrothed}\ n\ n$ says $\sigma(n) = 2n + 1$, i.e. that $n$ is quasiperfect, which is the separate open problem `QuasiperfectNumbers.exists_quasiperfect`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

