@decl BingBorsuk.bing_borsuk_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: The Bing-Borsuk Conjecture: every $n$-dimensional homogeneous absolute neighborhood retract is a topological $n$-manifold
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Bing-Borsuk Conjecture: every $n$-dimensional homogeneous absolute neighborhood retract is a topological $n$-manifold. A topological space $X$ is an $n$-dimensional manifold when `T2Space X ∧ Nonempty (ChartedSpace (Fin n → ℝ) X)`. The hypothesis `[MetrizableSpace X]` implies `T2Space X` so this does not appear in the conclusion.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

