-- L4DEL: intuition: **Borsuk's conjecture**, open range: every bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}^n$ with at least two points can be partitioned into $n + 1$ sets of strictly smaller diameter, for $4 \leq n \leq 62$. The conjecture is known to be true for $n \leq 3$ and false for $n \geq 63$.
