-- L4DEL: intuition: **Partial result in dimension $4$**: every bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}^4$ with at least two points can be partitioned into $8$ sets of strictly smaller diameter. Claimed by Tolmachev and Voronov [TV26] via computer-assisted partitions of a truncated Lassak cover, with floating-point verification; the preprint is not yet refereed.
