-- L4DEL: intuition: **Partial result in dimension $4$**: every bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}^4$ with at least two points can be partitioned into $9$ sets of strictly smaller diameter. Proved by Lassak [La82], who showed more generally that $2^{n-1} + 1$ parts suffice in $\mathbb{R}^n$.
