@decl DedekindNumber.kisielewiczFormula
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: kisielewiczFormula
-- L4DEL: intuition: A closed formula for the Dedekind numbers as found by Kisielewicz (1998): $$ M(n) = \sum_{k=0}^{2^{2^n}}\prod_{j = 1}^{2 ^ n - 1}\prod_{i = 0}^{j - 1} \left( 1 - b_i^kb_j^k \prod_{m = 0}^{\log_2 i} (1 - b_m^i + b_m^ib_m^j)\right), $$, where $b_i^k$ is the $i$-th bit of $k$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

