@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/DeterminantalConjecture.lean
@decl DeterminantalConjecture.determinantal_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: determinantal_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: Does the determinant of the sum $A + B$ of two $n \times n$ normal complex matrices $A$ and $B$ always lie in the convex hull of the $n!$ points $\prod\_i (\lambda(A)\_i + \lambda(B)\_{\sigma(i)})$? Here the numbers $\lambda(A)\_i$ and $\lambda(B)\_i$ are the eigenvalues of $A$ and $B$, and $\sigma$ is an element of the symmetric group $S\_n$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/DiameterSimpleFiniteGroups.lean
@decl BabaiSeressConjectures.babai_seress_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: babai_seress_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Babai–Seress Conjecture (Conjecture 1.7)**: There exists an absolute constant $C$ such that every finite simple non-abelian group $G$ satisfies $$\operatorname{diam}(G) \leq (\log |G|)^C.$$ *Reference:* L. Babai and Á. Seress, *On the diameter of permutation groups*, European Journal of Combinatorics 13 (1992), Conjecture 1.780029-0)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/DiameterSimpleFiniteGroups.lean
@decl BabaiSeressConjectures.babai_seress_conjecture_alternating
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: babai_seress_conjecture_alternating
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Babai–Seress Conjecture (Conjecture 1.5)**: There exists an absolute constant $C$ such that the diameter of the alternating group $A_n$ satisfies $$\operatorname{diam}(A_n) \leq n^C.$$ *Reference:* L. Babai and Á. Seress, *On the diameter of permutation groups*, European Journal of Combinatorics 13 (1992), Conjecture 1.580029-0)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/DiameterSimpleFiniteGroups.lean
@decl BabaiSeressConjectures.cayleyGraph
-- L4DEL: title: The (undirected) Cayley graph of a group $G$ with respect to a generating set $S$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The (undirected) Cayley graph of a group $G$ with respect to a generating set $S$. Two elements $g, h \in G$ are adjacent iff $g \neq h$ and $g^{-1} h \in S$ or $h^{-1} g \in S$. This is constructed using `SimpleGraph.fromRel`, which takes the relation $g \sim h \iff g^{-1} h \in S$ and automatically symmetrizes it (via disjunction with the reverse relation) and enforces irreflexivity (via $g \neq h$). In particular, this definition effectively uses the symmetrization $S \cup S^{-1}$, so it produces a standard undirected Cayley graph even when $S$ is not itself symmetric.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/DiameterSimpleFiniteGroups.lean
