@decl ElliottHalberstamConjecture.E
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: E
-- L4DEL: intuition: The error term $$E(x; q) = \max_{\gcd(a,q)=1} \left|\pi(x;q,a) - \frac{\pi(x)}{\varphi(q)}\right|,$$ measuring the deviation of the primes in the arithmetic progressions modulo $q$ from uniform distribution among the $\varphi(q)$ coprime residue classes.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/ElliottHalberstamConjecture.lean
@decl ElliottHalberstamConjecture.elliott_halberstam
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: elliott_halberstam
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Elliott–Halberstam conjecture: for every $\theta < 1$ and $A > 0$ there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that $$\sum_{1 \le q \le x^{\theta}} E(x; q) \le \frac{C x}{\log^A x}$$ for all $x > 2$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

