@decl EllipticCurveRank.RatEllipticCurve.rank_height_count_asymptotic
-- L4DEL: title: [PPVW2016] 8.2(b): for 1 ≤ r ≤ 20, the number of elliptic curves over ℚ with rank at least `r` and naïve height at most `H` is asymptotically `H ^ ((21 - r) / 24 + o(1))`
-- L4DEL: intuition: [PPVW2016] 8.2(b): for 1 ≤ r ≤ 20, the number of elliptic curves over ℚ with rank at least `r` and naïve height at most `H` is asymptotically `H ^ ((21 - r) / 24 + o(1))`. Note: ℰ_H in 8.2(b) should be ℰ_{≤H}, see the statement of Theorem 7.3.3. When `r = 1`, the exponent is `20 / 24 = 5 / 6`, which agrees with the exponent in `card_heightLE_div_pow_five_div_six_tensto` and is consistent with `half_rank_zero_and_half_rank_one`. The equality is asserted only for large `H`, matching the `o(1)` above: it cannot hold at small `H`, because `heightLE H` is empty for `H ≤ 3` (`naiveHeight E ≤ 3` forces `A = B = 0`, which both `Δ_ne_zero` and `reduced` exclude) and consists only of the two rank-zero curves `y² = x³ ± x` for `4 ≤ H ≤ 26`, while the right hand side is `Real.rpow` and hence strictly positive.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

