@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/FortuneConjecture.lean
@decl FortuneConjecture.fortunateNumber
-- L4DEL: title: The $n$-th *Fortunate number* (0-indexed): the smallest integer $m > 1$ such that $p_{n+1}\\# + m$ is prime
-- L4DEL: intuition: The $n$-th *Fortunate number* (0-indexed): the smallest integer $m > 1$ such that $p_{n+1}\\# + m$ is prime. `Nat.nth Nat.Prime n` is the $(n+1)$-st prime (0-indexed), and `primorial p` is the product of all primes $\le p$; when $p$ is the $(n+1)$-st prime this equals the product of the first $n+1$ primes. Thus `fortunateNumber 0` corresponds to $F_1 = 3$ in the OEIS A005235 indexing.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

