@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/GoodmanConjecture.lean
@decl GoodmanConjecture.goodman_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: goodman_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Goodman's conjecture.** For every $p$-valent normalised function $f$ on the unit disk and every $n > p$, the $n$-th coefficient is bounded by the Goodman bound: $$|b_n| \le \sum_{k=1}^{p} \frac{2k (n+p)!}{(p-k)!\,(p+k)!\,(n-p-1)!\,(n^2-k^2)} |b_k|.$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/GoodmanConjecture.lean
@decl GoodmanConjecture.goodmanBound
-- L4DEL: title: The Goodman bound $$\sum_{k=1}^{p} \frac{2k (n+p)!}{(p-k)!\,(p+k)!\,(n-p-1)!\,(n^2-k^2)} |b_k|,$$ the conjectured upper bound for $|b_n|$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Goodman bound $$\sum_{k=1}^{p} \frac{2k (n+p)!}{(p-k)!\,(p+k)!\,(n-p-1)!\,(n^2-k^2)} |b_k|,$$ the conjectured upper bound for $|b_n|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/GoodmanConjecture.lean
@decl GoodmanConjecture.goodmanBound_one
-- L4DEL: title: Sanity check: in the univalent case $p = 1$, the Goodman bound reduces to the classical Bieberbach-type bound $|b_n| \le n\,|b_1|$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Sanity check: in the univalent case $p = 1$, the Goodman bound reduces to the classical Bieberbach-type bound $|b_n| \le n\,|b_1|$. Concretely the single $k = 1$ summand is $$\frac{2 (n+1)!}{0!\,2!\,(n-2)!\,(n^2-1)} = \frac{(n+1)!}{(n-2)!\,(n^2-1)} = n,$$ so the bound equals $n\,|b_1|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

