@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/GoodmanConjecture.lean
@decl GoodmanConjecture.IsPValent
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsPValent
-- L4DEL: intuition: A function `f : ℂ → ℂ` is **$p$-valent** on the open unit disk $\mathbb{D} = \{z : |z| < 1\}$ if it is analytic there, attains every value at most $p$ times, and attains some value exactly $p$ times. Here $p \ge 1$. Values are counted at distinct points. For a non-constant analytic function this agrees with counting with multiplicity: near a point where $f - w$ has a zero of order $m$, every value close to $w$ is attained at $m$ distinct points, so the maximal number of distinct preimages equals the maximal number of preimages counted with multiplicity.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

