-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: growthFunction_not_polynomial_of_infinite
-- L4DEL: intuition: Infinite groups do not satisfy polynomial growth over `ℕ` for any degree `d` because when `d = 0` this reduces to the unbounded nature of `growthFunction` while `n = 0` works when `d ≠ 0`. Thus a finitely-generated infinite nilpotent group would be a counter-example to Gromov's theorem when quantifying over all of `ℕ`, and so `n = 0` should be excluded.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

