@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/HardyLittlewood.lean
@decl HardyLittlewood.first_hardy_littlewood_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Let $P = (m_1, \dots, m_k)$ be a tuple of distinct positive even integers
-- L4DEL: intuition: Let $P = (m_1, \dots, m_k)$ be a tuple of distinct positive even integers. Let $\pi_P(n)$ denote the number of primes $p\leq n$ such that $(p, p + m_1, \dots, p + m_k)$ forms an admissible prime constellation. Let $w(q; m_1, \dots, m_k)$ denote the number of distinct residues of $0, m_1, \dots, m_k$ modulo $q$, and let $$ C_P = 2 ^ k\prod_{\substack{q\ \text{prime} \\ q\geq 3}} \frac{1 - \frac{w(q; m_1, \dots, m_k)}{q}}{\left(1 - \frac{1}{q}\right)^{k+1}}. $$ Then $$ \pi_P(n)\sim C_P\int_2^n\frac{dt}{\log^{k+1}t}. $$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/HardyLittlewood.lean
@decl HardyLittlewood.FirstHardyLittlewoodConjectureFor
