@decl LovaszPlummerConjecture.sheehan_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Sheehan's conjecture (1977).** Every $4$-regular graph with a Hamiltonian cycle has a second Hamiltonian cycle (one with a different edge set)
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Sheehan's conjecture (1977).** Every $4$-regular graph with a Hamiltonian cycle has a second Hamiltonian cycle (one with a different edge set). Sheehan's conjecture would settle the last open case of the question, raised by Smith's theorem for cubic graphs, of which regular Hamiltonian graphs have a second Hamiltonian cycle: Thomassen [Th98] proved it for all $r$-regular graphs with $r \ge 300$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

