@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MeanValueProblem.lean
@decl MeanValueProblem.mean_value_problem
-- L4DEL: title: Given a complex polynomial $p$ of degree $d ≥ 2$ and a complex number $z$ there is a critical point $c$ of $p$, such that $|p(z)-p(c)|/|z-c| ≤ |p'(z)|$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Given a complex polynomial $p$ of degree $d ≥ 2$ and a complex number $z$ there is a critical point $c$ of $p$, such that $|p(z)-p(c)|/|z-c| ≤ |p'(z)|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MeanValueProblem.lean
@decl MeanValueProblem.mean_value_problem_leq_4
-- L4DEL: title: The following weaker version of the mean value problem has been proven
-- L4DEL: intuition: The following weaker version of the mean value problem has been proven. Given a complex polynomial $p$ of degree $d ≥ 2$ and a complex number $z$ there a critical point $c$ of $p$, such that $|p(z)-p(c)|/|z-c| ≤ 4|p'(z)|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MeanValueProblem.lean
@decl MeanValueProblem.mean_value_problem_of_real_roots
-- L4DEL: title: The following tighter bound depending on the degree $d$ of the polynomial $p$ has been shown by Tischler
-- L4DEL: intuition: The following tighter bound depending on the degree $d$ of the polynomial $p$ has been shown by Tischler. Let $z$ be a complex number such that the normalised polynomial $p(X + z) - p(z)$ has only real roots, i.e. every $x$ with $p(x) = p(z)$ satisfies $\operatorname{Im} x = \operatorname{Im} z$. Then there is a critical point $c$ of $p$ such that $|p(z)-p(c)|/|z-c| \le (d-1)/d \cdot |p'(z)|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/MeanValueProblem.lean
@decl MeanValueProblem.mean_value_problem_of_roots_same_norm
-- L4DEL: title: The following tighter bound depending on the degree $d$ of the polynomial $p$ has been shown by Tischler
-- L4DEL: intuition: The following tighter bound depending on the degree $d$ of the polynomial $p$ has been shown by Tischler. Let $z$ be a complex number such that all nonzero roots of the normalised polynomial $p(X + z) - p(z)$ have the same norm, i.e. all $x \ne z$ with $p(x) = p(z)$ have the same distance to $z$. Then there is a critical point $c$ of $p$ such that $|p(z) - p(c)|/|z-c| \le (d-1)/d \cdot |p'(z)|$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

