-- L4DEL: intuition: Gerver's sofa is the unique sofa that attains the sofa constant, up to a rigid motion. The motion is needed: `horizontalHallway` is $(-\infty, 1] \times [0, 1]$, so a leftward translate of any moving sofa is again one, obtained by sliding right and then following the original motion. It has the same area, so uniqueness cannot hold on the nose.
