@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/NoetherProblem.lean
@decl NoetherProblem.HasNoetherProperty
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasNoetherProperty
-- L4DEL: intuition: We say that a rational extension `L` of `K` in the indeterminates `ι` has the _Noether Property_ if, for every identification of `L` with the rational function field `K(X_i : i ∈ ι)`, the fixed field `L^H` of every group `H` of `K`-automorphisms of `L` permuting the indeterminates `X_i` is again a rational extension of `K`. Such a group `H` is necessarily finite.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

