@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/NoetherProblem.lean
@decl NoetherProblem.noether_problem
-- L4DEL: title: The **Noether Problem**: let `L` be the field of rational functions in `n` indeterminates over `K`, and let `G` be a finite group permuting these indeterminates
-- L4DEL: intuition: The **Noether Problem**: let `L` be the field of rational functions in `n` indeterminates over `K`, and let `G` be a finite group permuting these indeterminates. Is the fixed field `L^G` a rational extension of `K`, i.e. does `L/K` have the Noether property? Solution: False.
