@decl PerfectNumbers.infinitely_many_even_perfect
-- L4DEL: title: Infinitely many even perfect numbers conjecture.** Are there infinitely many even perfect numbers?
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Infinitely many even perfect numbers conjecture.** Are there infinitely many even perfect numbers? This is equivalent to asking whether there are infinitely many Mersenne primes, since by the Euclid–Euler theorem an even number is perfect if and only if it has the form $2^{p-1}(2^p - 1)$ where $2^p - 1$ is a Mersenne prime. *Reference:* Wikipedia
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

