-- L4DEL: intuition: A known result: If an odd perfect number exists, it must be of the form $p^α * m^2$ where $p$ is prime, $p \equiv 1 \pmod{4}$, $\alpha \equiv 1 \pmod{4}$, and $p \nmid m$. *Reference:* Euler's theorem on odd perfect numbers. Formal proof linked here provided by AlphaProof.
