@decl PowerfulNumbersDensity.asymptotic_bateman_grosswald
-- L4DEL: title: Bateman and Grosswald [BG58] proved the sharper asymptotic $$Q(x) = \frac{\zeta(3/2)}{\zeta(3)} x^{1/2} + \frac{\zeta(2/3)}{\zeta(2)} x^{1/3} + O(x^{1/6}).$$
-- L4DEL: intuition: Bateman and Grosswald [BG58] proved the sharper asymptotic $$Q(x) = \frac{\zeta(3/2)}{\zeta(3)} x^{1/2} + \frac{\zeta(2/3)}{\zeta(2)} x^{1/3} + O(x^{1/6}).$$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/PowerfulNumbersDensity.lean
@decl PowerfulNumbersDensity.asymptotic_erdos_szekeres
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: asymptotic_erdos_szekeres
-- L4DEL: intuition: Erdős and Szekeres [ES35] proved that the number of powerful integers up to $x$ satisfies $$Q(x) = \frac{\zeta(3/2)}{\zeta(3)} x^{1/2} + O(x^{1/3}).$$ In particular $Q(x) \sim \frac{\zeta(3/2)}{\zeta(3)} \sqrt{x}$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

