-- L4DEL: intuition: Can the exponent $1/6$ in the error term of the Bateman–Grosswald asymptotic be improved unconditionally? That is, is there $\delta > 0$ such that $$Q(x) = \frac{\zeta(3/2)}{\zeta(3)} x^{1/2} + \frac{\zeta(2/3)}{\zeta(2)} x^{1/3} + O(x^{1/6 - \delta})?$$ Improvements are known under the Riemann Hypothesis.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

