@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/RudinsConjecture.lean
@decl RudinsConjecture.rudins_conjecture_unique
-- L4DEL: title: The strongest form of Rudin's conjecture also asserts *uniqueness*: for $N \ge 6$, any non-trivial arithmetic progression attaining the maximum $Q(N)$ has common difference $24$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The strongest form of Rudin's conjecture also asserts *uniqueness*: for $N \ge 6$, any non-trivial arithmetic progression attaining the maximum $Q(N)$ has common difference $24$. (Its initial term is then forced by $\gcd(24, a) = 1$; the progression $24n + 1$ is the canonical representative.)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

