@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/Selfridge.lean
@decl Selfridge.IsPseudoSelfridge
-- L4DEL: title: A number `p` satisfies the *Pseudo Selfridge condition* if 1
-- L4DEL: intuition: A number `p` satisfies the *Pseudo Selfridge condition* if 1. `p` is odd, 2. `p ≡ ± 1 (mod 5)`, 3. `2^(p-1) ≡ 1 (mod p)` 4. `(p-1).fib ≡ 0 (mod p)` This is a variant of the condition that is tested in the PSW conjecture, and appears in the wiki page mentioned above. Note: this is non-standard terminology.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/Selfridge.lean
@decl Selfridge.IsSelfridge
