-- L4DEL: intuition: Selfridge's test variant: Let $p$ be an odd number, with $p \equiv \pm 1 \pmod{5}$, $2^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p}$ and $F_{p-1} \equiv 0 \pmod{p}$, then $p$ is a prime number. This test does not work.
