-- L4DEL: intuition: Selfridge's test variant: Let $p$ be an odd number, with $p \equiv \pm 1 \pmod{5}$, $2^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p}$ and $F_{p-1} \equiv 0 \pmod{p}$, then $p$ is a prime number. The number $6601$ is a conterexample to this test satisfying $6601 ≡ 1 \mod 5$
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

