@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/Sendov.lean
@decl Sendov.sendov_conjecture.variants.eventually_true
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: eventually_true
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Sendov's conjecture** states that for a polynomial $$f(z)=(z-r_{1})\cdots (z-r_{n}),\qquad (n\geq 2)$$ with all roots $r_1, ..., r_n$ inside the closed unit disk $|z| ≤ 1$, each of the $n$ roots is at a distance no more than $1$ from at least one critical point. It has been shown that Sendov's conjecture holds for polynomials of sufficiently large degree.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/Sendov.lean
