@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SerreMultiplicityConjectures.lean
@decl SerreMultiplicityConjectures.intersectionMultiplicity_eq_zero_of_lt
-- L4DEL: title: Vanishing.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Vanishing.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length. If $\dim M + \dim N < \dim R$, then $\chi(M, N) = 0$. Conjectured by Serre and proved by Roberts [Ro85] and, independently, by Gillet and Soulé [GS87].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SerreMultiplicityConjectures.lean
@decl SerreMultiplicityConjectures.intersectionMultiplicity_nonneg
-- L4DEL: title: Non-negativity.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Non-negativity.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length. Then $\chi(M, N) \ge 0$. Conjectured by Serre and proved by Gabber in 1995 [Ro98].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SerreMultiplicityConjectures.lean
@decl SerreMultiplicityConjectures.intersectionMultiplicity_pos
-- L4DEL: title: Positivity conjecture.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Positivity conjecture.** Let $R$ be a regular local ring and let $M$, $N$ be finitely generated $R$-modules such that $M \otimes_R N$ has finite length. If $\dim M + \dim N = \dim R$, then $\chi(M, N) > 0$. The hypothesis on dimensions forces $M$ and $N$ to be nonzero, since the dimension of the zero module is $\bot$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SerreMultiplicityConjectures.lean
