@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: sidorenko_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Sidorenko's conjecture (1993).** For every finite bipartite simple graph $H$ and every finite simple graph $G$: $t(H, G) \ge t(K_2, G)^{e(H)}$, where $K_2$ denotes the single-edge graph on 2 vertices (i.e. `completeGraph (Fin 2)`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture.variants.complete_bipartite
-- L4DEL: title: Case: complete bipartite graphs `K_{s,t}` (Sidorenko 1993).** Sidorenko's inequality holds when `H = K_{s,t}` is a complete bipartite graph
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Case: complete bipartite graphs `K_{s,t}` (Sidorenko 1993).** Sidorenko's inequality holds when `H = K_{s,t}` is a complete bipartite graph. This is one of the earliest known cases; it follows from repeated applications of the Cauchy–Schwarz / Hölder inequality. The `s = t = 2` instance is `sidorenko_K22`. *Reference:* [Si93].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture.variants.even_cycle
-- L4DEL: title: Case: even cycles `C_{2k}` (Sidorenko 1993).** Sidorenko's inequality holds for every even cycle `C_{2k}` with `k ≥ 2` (`cycleGraph (2 * k)`)
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Case: even cycles `C_{2k}` (Sidorenko 1993).** Sidorenko's inequality holds for every even cycle `C_{2k}` with `k ≥ 2` (`cycleGraph (2 * k)`). Even cycles are bipartite; the `k = 2` case `C_4` coincides with `K_{2,2}` (`sidorenko_K22`). *Reference:* [Si93].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture.variants.non_bipartite_necessary
-- L4DEL: title: Bipartiteness is necessary: the triangle is not a Sidorenko graph.** The hypothesis `H.IsBipartite` in `sidorenko_conjecture` cannot be dropped
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Bipartiteness is necessary: the triangle is not a Sidorenko graph.** The hypothesis `H.IsBipartite` in `sidorenko_conjecture` cannot be dropped. For the triangle `H = K_3` (chromatic number `3`, hence not bipartite) and the single edge `G = K_2`, Sidorenko's inequality fails: the putative lower bound is `t(K_2, K_2)^{e(K_3)} = (1/2)^3 = 1/8`, while the actual density is `t(K_3, K_2) = 0`, because there is no graph homomorphism from `K_3` into the triangle-free graph `K_2` (such a homomorphism would be an injection `Fin 3 ↪ Fin 2`). So the lower bound `1/8` strictly exceeds the true value `0`. More generally, any `H` containing an odd cycle fails Sidorenko's inequality against a suitable bipartite `G`, since then `t(H, G) = 0 < t(K_2, G)^{e(H)}`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture.variants.path_blakley_roy
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: path_blakley_roy
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Case: paths, the Blakley–Roy inequality (1965).** For the path `P_n` on `n` vertices (`pathGraph n`), Sidorenko's inequality `t(K_2, G)^{e(P_n)} ≤ t(P_n, G)` is the Blakley–Roy inequality, established well before Sidorenko's general conjecture. Paths are trees, so this is also a special case of `sidorenko_tree`. *Reference:* [BR65].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture.variants.star
-- L4DEL: title: Case: stars `K_{1,m}` (Sidorenko).** Sidorenko's inequality holds for every star `K_{1,m} = completeBipartiteGraph (Fin 1) (Fin m)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Case: stars `K_{1,m}` (Sidorenko).** Sidorenko's inequality holds for every star `K_{1,m} = completeBipartiteGraph (Fin 1) (Fin m)`. This is a fully proved instance of both `sidorenko_conjecture.variants.complete_bipartite` and `sidorenko_tree` (a star is a complete bipartite graph and a tree). **Proof.** With `d(c) := G.degree c` and `N := |W|`, the star has `m` edges, so the desired inequality is `(∑_c d(c) / N^2)^m ≤ (∑_c d(c)^m) / N^{m+1}` (using `t(K_2, G) = ∑_c d(c) / N^2` and `t(K_{1,m}, G) = ∑_c d(c)^m / N^{m+1}` via `homCount_star_eq_sum_degree_pow`). After clearing denominators this is `(∑_c d(c))^m ≤ N^{m-1} · ∑_c d(c)^m`, the power-mean (Jensen) inequality `Finset.pow_sum_div_card_le_sum_pow`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SidorenkoConjecture.lean
@decl SidorenkoConjecture.sidorenko_conjecture_graphon
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: sidorenko_conjecture_graphon
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Sidorenko's conjecture for graphons (1993).** For every finite bipartite simple graph $H$ and every graphon $W$ on $[0, 1]$ with Lebesgue measure: $t(H, W) \ge t(K_2, W)^{e(H)}$, where $t(K_2, W) = p(W)$ is the edge density of $W$, and $t(H, W)$ is the graphon homomorphism density of $H$ in $W$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

