@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SixStandardDeviations.lean
@decl SixStandardDeviations.six_standard_deviations
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: six_standard_deviations
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Six standard deviations suffice** (Spencer, 1985) For every $n$ and every family of $n$ subsets $S_1, \dots, S_n$ of $\{1, \dots, n\}$, there is a colouring $\chi : \{1, \dots, n\} \to \{-1, +1\}$ such that $\left|\sum_{j \in S_i} \chi(j)\right| \le 6\sqrt{n}$ for every $i$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

