-- L4DEL: intuition: A ruler is *complete* (a perfect ruler) if its marks form a difference basis for $\{0, 1, \ldots, L\}$, i.e. every distance $k \le L$ is the difference of two marks. This is `Finset.IsDifferenceBasis` applied to the marks.
