-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SteinerSystem.lean
@decl SteinerSystems.SteinerSystem
-- L4DEL: title: An $S(t, k, n)$-Steiner system is a collection of $k$-element subsets (called blocks) of $\{0, \ldots, n-1\}$ such that every $t$-element subset is contained in exactly one block
-- L4DEL: intuition: An $S(t, k, n)$-Steiner system is a collection of $k$-element subsets (called blocks) of $\{0, \ldots, n-1\}$ such that every $t$-element subset is contained in exactly one block. This is the standard notation from combinatorics, where: - $n$ is the number of points - $k$ is the block size - $t$ is the covering parameter (every $t$-subset is in exactly one block)
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

