@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/SurjunctiveGroup.lean
@decl GottschalkSurjunctivity.shift
-- L4DEL: title: The left shift of `x : G → A` by `g : G`, defined by `(shift g x)(h) = x(g⁻¹ * h)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The left shift of `x : G → A` by `g : G`, defined by `(shift g x)(h) = x(g⁻¹ * h)`. This is the standard left shift action of `G` on `A^G`. We define it as a plain function rather than a `MulAction` instance to avoid conflict with the pointwise `Pi.instMulAction`.
