@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/VizingConjecture.lean
@decl VizingConjecture.vizing_conjecture
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: vizing_conjecture
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Vizing's conjecture (1968).** For all finite simple graphs $G$ and $H$, the domination number of the Cartesian (box) product satisfies $\gamma(G \,\square\, H) \ge \gamma(G)\,\gamma(H)$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/VizingConjecture.lean
@decl VizingConjecture.vizing_conjecture.variants.clark_suen
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: clark_suen
-- L4DEL: intuition: **The Clark–Suen inequality (2000).** For all finite simple graphs $G$ and $H$, $\gamma(G \,\square\, H) \ge \tfrac12\,\gamma(G)\,\gamma(H)$; that is, Vizing's conjecture holds up to a factor of $2$. *Reference:* [ClSu00].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/VizingConjecture.lean
@decl VizingConjecture.vizing_conjecture.variants.dominationNumber_eq_one
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: dominationNumber_eq_one
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Vizing's conjecture when `γ(H) = 1`.** If `H` has a dominating vertex, so that $\gamma(H) = 1$, then Vizing's inequality reduces to $\gamma(G) \le \gamma(G \,\square\, H)$, which is the projection bound `dominationNumber_le_dominationNumber_boxProd`. This is the simplest of the known cases of the conjecture (see [BDGHHKR12]).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/Wikipedia/VizingConjecture.lean
@decl VizingConjecture.vizing_conjecture.variants.suen_tarr
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: suen_tarr
-- L4DEL: intuition: **The Suen–Tarr inequality (2012).** For all finite simple graphs $G$ and $H$, $\gamma(G \,\square\, H) \ge \tfrac12\,\gamma(G)\,\gamma(H) + \tfrac12\min\{\gamma(G), \gamma(H)\}$, improving the Clark–Suen bound. *Reference:* [SuTa12].
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

