-- L4DEL: intuition: For any given integer $a > 0$, are there infinitely many primes $p$ such that $a^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p^2}$? The case $a = 1$ is trivial, since every prime qualifies (`isWieferichPrimeBase_one_iff`). So is the case $a = 0$ under our definition (`isWieferichPrimeBase_zero_iff`), which is why the source's restriction to $a > 0$ is dropped.
