@file FormalConjectures/WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture291.lean
@decl WrittenOnTheWallII.GraphConjecture291.havelHakimiZeroStep
-- L4DEL: title: The first step $i$ (counting from $0$) at which a zero appears in the Havel-Hakimi reduction of the descending degree sequence of $G$, or in which the sequence has been emptied
-- L4DEL: intuition: The first step $i$ (counting from $0$) at which a zero appears in the Havel-Hakimi reduction of the descending degree sequence of $G$, or in which the sequence has been emptied. We use `sInf` over the set of such $i$ so the definition is well-defined for every graph: in particular, when $G$ is a connected graph with $n \ge 2$ the minimum degree at iteration $0$ is at least $1$, so the first zero only appears at some $i \ge 1$; and since each step strictly shortens the list (or empties it), at the latest by $i = n$ the sequence is empty and the predicate holds vacuously. This is the WOWII $k$ of Conjecture 291, which is the **first** step at which a zero appears — typically strictly less than $n - \mathrm{residue}(G)$ (which is the *total* number of reduction steps to reach the all-zero state).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

