@file FormalConjectures/WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture314.lean
@decl WrittenOnTheWallII.GraphConjecture314.conjecture314
-- L4DEL: title: WOWII Conjecture 314: For every finite simple connected graph $G$ with $n > 1$ vertices, if $G$ is triangle-free and $\mathrm{path}(G) \le 4$, then $G$ is well totally dominated
-- L4DEL: intuition: WOWII Conjecture 314: For every finite simple connected graph $G$ with $n > 1$ vertices, if $G$ is triangle-free and $\mathrm{path}(G) \le 4$, then $G$ is well totally dominated. Here $\mathrm{path}(G) = \mathrm{largestInducedPathSize}\, G$ is the **size of a largest induced path** in $G$, defined locally above. **Disambiguation.** Earlier revisions of this file used the `SimpleGraph.path` invariant, but that is the *floor of the average distance*, not the size of a largest induced path — a different quantity that makes Conjecture 314 vacuous in many cases. **Proof summary.** In a connected, $K_{3}$-free, induced-$P_{5}$-free graph $G$: 1. No minimal total dominating set has fewer than two vertices. 2. No minimal total dominating set has more than three vertices. 3. Minimal total dominating sets of sizes two and three cannot coexist. Thus, each minimal total dominating set in $G$ has the same size. The Lean proof was generated by OpenAI GPT-5.6 Sol.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjectures/WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture314.lean
@decl WrittenOnTheWallII.GraphConjecture314.largestInducedPathSize
-- L4DEL: title: The size of a largest induced path of $G$, as a natural number
-- L4DEL: intuition: The size of a largest induced path of $G$, as a natural number. A subset $s \subseteq V(G)$ is an *induced path* when the induced subgraph `G.induce s` is a tree in which every vertex has degree at most $2$ (equivalently: a tree that is itself a path graph). We define `largestInducedPathSize G` as the supremum of `s.card` over all such subsets. **Disambiguation.** This is *not* the `SimpleGraph.path` invariant, which is the floor of the average distance — that one is the wrong tool for WOWII Conjecture 314, where $\mathrm{path}(G)$ denotes the **size of a largest induced path**. TODO: it would probably be clearer to rename the `SimpleGraph.path` invariant to something like `pathBound` / `floorAvgDist` to avoid this naming collision.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

