@file FormalConjectures/WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture322.lean
@decl WrittenOnTheWallII.GraphConjecture322.conjecture322
-- L4DEL: title: WOWII Conjecture 322 Let `G` be a simple connected graph on `n ≥ 5` vertices
-- L4DEL: intuition: WOWII Conjecture 322 Let `G` be a simple connected graph on `n ≥ 5` vertices. If the maximum over all vertices `v` of `l(v)` in the complement graph `Gᶜ` — the independence number of the neighborhood `N(v)` of `v` — is at most 1, then `G` is well totally dominated. Here `l(v) = α(Gᶜ[N(v)])` is the independence number of the subgraph induced by the open neighborhood of `v` in `Gᶜ`. This proof was provided by Samuel Schlesinger.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

