@file FormalConjectures/WrittenOnTheWallII/GraphConjecture33.lean
@decl WrittenOnTheWallII.GraphConjecture33.conjecture33
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: conjecture33
-- L4DEL: intuition: WOWII Conjecture 33 For a simple connected graph $G$, $\operatorname{path}(G) \ge \lceil 2 \operatorname{dist}\_{\operatorname{avg}}(M, V) \rceil$, where $\operatorname{path}(G)$ is the number of vertices of a largest induced path of $G$, $M$ is the set of maximum-degree vertices, and $\operatorname{dist}\_{\operatorname{avg}}(M, V)$ is the average of all nonzero distances $\operatorname{dist}\_G(m, v)$ with $m \in M$ and $v \in V$. The conjecture is false: the source records an October 2005 counterexample with $\operatorname{path}(G) = 7$ and $\operatorname{dist}\_{\operatorname{avg}}(M, V) = 3.56$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

