@decl WeierstrassCurve.realPeriod
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: realPeriod
-- L4DEL: intuition: **The real period as an integral**: the integral of $|\omega|$ over the real locus $E(\mathbb{R})$, that is $2 \int_{\mathbb{R}} dx / \sqrt{F(x)}$ with the integrand taken to be $0$ where $F \leq 0$. This is the real period of the Birch and Swinnerton-Dyer conjecture, in the convention that absorbs the real Tamagawa number.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

