-- L4DEL: intuition: The greedy Sidon set in `{1, …, N}`: starting from `∅`, iterate through `1, …, N` and include `x` if and only if `A ∪ {x}` remains Sidon. Alternatively, this is precisely the set of elements in the greedy Sidon sequence that are `≤ N`.
