@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics._root_.Combinatorics.hypergraphRamsey_two_le_four_pow
-- L4DEL: title: Erdős–Szekeres 1935** in `hypergraphRamsey` form: `Combinatorics.hypergraphRamsey 2 k ≤ 4 ^ k` for all `k`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Erdős–Szekeres 1935** in `hypergraphRamsey` form: `Combinatorics.hypergraphRamsey 2 k ≤ 4 ^ k` for all `k`. **Proof.** `Diagonal.hasRamseyProperty_choose` applied at `s = t = k` and the full vertex set `V = Finset.univ` of `Fin (C(2k, k))` shows that `C(2k, k)` is a member of the defining set of `hypergraphRamsey 2 k`, hence by `Nat.sInf_le` we get `hypergraphRamsey 2 k ≤ C(2k, k)`; the central binomial bound `C(2k, k) ≤ 4 ^ k` closes the result.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.card_false_true_split
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: card_false_true_split
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Pigeonhole step: splitting `V \ {v}` by colour.** For any vertex `v ∈ V`, the set `V.erase v` partitions into `false`-neighbours of `v` and `true`-neighbours of `v`, and the cardinalities sum to `V.card - 1`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.forall_two_subset_singleton
-- L4DEL: title: A singleton has no 2-element subsets, hence is monochromatic of any colour
-- L4DEL: intuition: A singleton has no 2-element subsets, hence is monochromatic of any colour.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.HasRamseyProperty
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasRamseyProperty
-- L4DEL: intuition: `HasRamseyProperty N s t` asserts: for every `m`, every coloring `c : Finset (Fin m) → Bool`, and every `V : Finset (Fin m)` with `V.card ≥ N`, the subset `V` contains either a subset of size `s` whose 2-element subsets are all `false`-coloured, or a subset of size `t` whose 2-element subsets are all `true`-coloured. This is the "off-diagonal Ramsey number does not exceed `N`" form of the classical Erdős–Szekeres Ramsey recurrence, packaged in the same shape used by `Combinatorics.hypergraphRamsey`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.HasRamseyProperty.mono
-- L4DEL: title: Monotonicity.** If `N ≤ N'` then `HasRamseyProperty N s t → HasRamseyProperty N' s t`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Monotonicity.** If `N ≤ N'` then `HasRamseyProperty N s t → HasRamseyProperty N' s t`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.HasRamseyProperty.step
-- L4DEL: title: Recurrence.** If `HasRamseyProperty Ns s (t+1)` and `HasRamseyProperty Nt (s+1) t` hold, then `HasRamseyProperty (Ns + Nt) (s+1) (t+1)` holds
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Recurrence.** If `HasRamseyProperty Ns s (t+1)` and `HasRamseyProperty Nt (s+1) t` hold, then `HasRamseyProperty (Ns + Nt) (s+1) (t+1)` holds. This is the core Erdős–Szekeres 1935 pigeonhole step: pick any vertex `v ∈ V`, split `V.erase v` into `false`-neighbours `R_v` and `true`-neighbours `B_v`; by pigeonhole `|R_v| ≥ Ns` or `|B_v| ≥ Nt`. In the first case, invoke `HasRamseyProperty Ns s (t+1)` on `R_v`: either we get a `false`-mono `K_s` on `R_v` (extend by `v` to a `false`-mono `K_{s+1}` on `V`), or a `true`-mono `K_{t+1}` on `R_v ⊆ V` (done). The second case is symmetric.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/Ramsey/Diagonal.lean
@decl Combinatorics.Diagonal.hasRamseyProperty_choose
-- L4DEL: title: Binomial bound via Erdős–Szekeres induction.** `HasRamseyProperty (Nat.choose (s + t) s) s t` for all `s, t`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Binomial bound via Erdős–Szekeres induction.** `HasRamseyProperty (Nat.choose (s + t) s) s t` for all `s, t`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

