@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/InducedTreeNeighborhood.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.maxDegree_add_girth_le_largestInducedTreeSize_add_three
-- L4DEL: title: Main counting theorem**: in a connected graph with a cycle and girth at least `4`, `Δ(G) + girth(G) ≤ largestInducedTreeSize G + 3`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Main counting theorem**: in a connected graph with a cycle and girth at least `4`, `Δ(G) + girth(G) ≤ largestInducedTreeSize G + 3`. Proof: grow a maximum induced tree `s` through the closed neighborhood of a maximum-degree vertex `v`; a boundary vertex `z` of `s` has two neighbors `a ≠ b` in `s`, and the tree path from `a` to `b` closes through `z` into a cycle, so it has at least `girth − 2` edges; the path meets the closed neighborhood of `v` in at most `3` vertices, so inclusion–exclusion inside `s` gives the bound.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

