@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/LovaszTheta.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.lovaszThetaFunction
-- L4DEL: title: Lovász Theta Function ($\vartheta(G)$)
-- L4DEL: intuition: Lovász Theta Function ($\vartheta(G)$). The Lovász theta function is defined as: $$\vartheta(G) = \min \lambda_{\max}(A)$$ where the minimum is taken over all real symmetric (Hermitian) matrices $A$ such that: * $A_{ii} = 1$ for all $i$ (diagonal entries are $1$), and * $A_{ij} = 1$ for all $\{i,j\} \notin E(G)$ (entries corresponding to non-edges are $1$). Here $\lambda_{\max}(A)$ denotes the maximum eigenvalue of $A$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

