@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Ramsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.graphRamsey
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: graphRamsey
-- L4DEL: intuition: The two-color Ramsey number `graphRamsey G H` is the minimum number of vertices `n` such that every 2-coloring of the edges of the complete graph on `n` vertices contains a copy of `G` in the first color or a copy of `H` in the second color. A 2-coloring of the complete graph on `Fin n` is represented by a graph `C` (the edges of the first color) and its complement `Cᶜ` (the edges of the second color).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Ramsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.HasCountableRamseyEscape
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasCountableRamseyEscape
-- L4DEL: intuition: The **countable Ramsey escape property** for the pair $(G_1, G_2)$: every $G_1$-free graph `H` on a `Type`-valued vertex type has a countable edge-colouring in which every colour class is $G_2$-free.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Ramsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.HasFiniteRamseyProperty
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasFiniteRamseyProperty
-- L4DEL: intuition: The **finite Ramsey property** for the pair $(G_1, G_2)$: for every $n \geq 1$, there exists a $G_1$-free graph `H` on some vertex type in `Type` (universe 0) such that every `n`-edge-colouring of `H` contains a monochromatic copy of `G_2`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Ramsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.IsErdosHajnalExceptional
-- L4DEL: title: A pair $(G_1, G_2)$ is **Erdős–Hajnal exceptional** if it has both the finite Ramsey property and the countable Ramsey escape property
