@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Ramsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.IsRamseySizeLinear
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsRamseySizeLinear
-- L4DEL: intuition: A graph `G` is **Ramsey size linear** if there exists a constant `c > 0` such that for all graphs `H` with `m` edges and no isolated vertices, the Ramsey number satisfies `R(G, H) ≤ c · m`. Note that this is about the (vertex) Ramsey number `graphRamsey G H`, not the size Ramsey number `sizeRamsey G H`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Residue.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.havelHakimiStep
-- L4DEL: title: Helper function: Performs one step of the Havel-Hakimi reduction on a degree sequence
-- L4DEL: intuition: Helper function: Performs one step of the Havel-Hakimi reduction on a degree sequence. Assumes the input list `s` is sorted descending. Removes the first element `d`, decrements the next `d` elements by 1, and re-sorts the list descending. Note: when `s` is the list of vertices arising from a simple graph, if the first index is `s` then the degree list always has length at least `s+1` so this makes sense.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Residue.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.havelHakimiStep_length_cons
-- L4DEL: title: `havelHakimiStep` drops the list length by exactly one on a nonempty list: `(havelHakimiStep (d :: rest)).length = rest.length`
-- L4DEL: intuition: `havelHakimiStep` drops the list length by exactly one on a nonempty list: `(havelHakimiStep (d :: rest)).length = rest.length`. `splitAt` partitions `rest`, and `map`, `++`, and `mergeSort` all preserve the total length while the head `d` is dropped. This is the termination measure for the well-founded `residueAux` below.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Residue.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.residue
-- L4DEL: title: Computes the residue of a graph `G`, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: Computes the residue of a graph `G`, i.e. the number of zeros remaining after iteratively applying the Havel-Hakimi algorithm to the degree sequence until all remaining degrees are zero. Starts with the descending degree sequence and applies the Havel-Hakimi process.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/Residue.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.residueAux
-- L4DEL: title: Auxiliary function to calculate the residue recursively
-- L4DEL: intuition: Auxiliary function to calculate the residue recursively. Applies Havel-Hakimi steps until the sequence consists only of zeros or is empty. Defined by well-founded recursion on the list length (via `havelHakimiStep_length_cons`), so that it admits equational and inductive reasoning.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

