@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Combinatorics/SimpleGraph/SizeRamsey.lean
@decl SimpleGraph.sizeRamsey
-- L4DEL: title: The size Ramsey number `r̂(G, H)` is the minimum number of edges in a graph `F` such that any 2-coloring of `F`'s edges contains a copy of `G` in one color or `H` in the other
-- L4DEL: intuition: The size Ramsey number `r̂(G, H)` is the minimum number of edges in a graph `F` such that any 2-coloring of `F`'s edges contains a copy of `G` in one color or `H` in the other. A 2-coloring is represented by a subgraph `R ≤ F` (the "red" edges); the "blue" edges are `F \ R`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

