@decl SimpleGraph.distAvgSet
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: distAvgSet
-- L4DEL: intuition: The average distance between distinct vertices of a set `S`: $\operatorname{dist}_{\operatorname{avg}}(S)$ is the mean of $\operatorname{dist}_G(u, v)$ over all ordered pairs $(u, v)$ of distinct vertices of $S$. Returns `0` when $S$ contains fewer than two vertices. This is DeLaVina's `dist_avg(S)` invariant ("average distance between maximum degree vertices" when `S = M`), used in WOWII conjecture 23. It is distinct from `distavg`, which averages the distances from *all* vertices of `G` to the set.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

