-- L4DEL: intuition: The **eccentricity of a set** `S`: the maximum, over all vertices `v` of `G`, of the minimum distance from `v` to any vertex in `S`. (This includes vertices in `S` itself, which contribute distance `0`.) Returns `0` when `S` is empty. Unlike `ecc`, which restricts the outer maximum to vertices `v ∉ S`, `eccSet` does not exclude any vertex; it is the conventional definition of "set eccentricity" used in DeLaVina's WOWII conjectures 142, 145 and 146.
