@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Computability/TuringMachine/Notation.lean
@decl mkStateType
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: mkStateType
-- L4DEL: intuition: `mkStateType n` adds to the environment an inductive type with `n` states names `State{n}` with constructors the symbols `A, B, ...`, together with the instance `Inhabited (State{n})`. Both declarations have to be `public`. `liftCommandElabM` runs them in a fresh scope that does not carry the surrounding module's visibility, so without it they are declared private and end up named `_private..0.State{n}`. The lookup below then fails with `Unknown constant State{n}`, and the type would in any case be private while appearing in the type of the term this elaborator returns.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

