@decl parseTuring
-- L4DEL: title: `parseTuring tmStringDescription` outputs the `Expr` corresponding to the Turing Machine described by the string `tmStringDescription`
-- L4DEL: intuition: `parseTuring tmStringDescription` outputs the `Expr` corresponding to the Turing Machine described by the string `tmStringDescription`. To do so, it 1) Runs `mkStateType` to add the state type to the environment 2) Defines the corresponding Turing Machine as a function using the `match` syntax. Warning: if a state type (i.e. something with the name `State1, State2, ...`) already exists in the environment then this will be reused without checking that this is the right inductive type - such checks are left to the user.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

