@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Data/Nat/PerfectPower.lean
@decl Nat.IsPerfectPower
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsPerfectPower
-- L4DEL: intuition: A perfect power is a natural number that is a product of equal natural factors, or, in other words, an integer that can be expressed as a square or a higher integer power of another integer greater than one. More formally, $n$ is a perfect power if there exist natural numbers $m > 1$, and $k > 1$ such that $m ^ k = n$. In this case, $n$ may be called a perfect $k$th power. If $k = 2$ or $k = 3$, then $n$ is called a perfect square or perfect cube, respectively.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

