@decl Set.HasDensity
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasDensity
-- L4DEL: intuition: A set `S` in an order `β` where all intervals bounded above are finite is said to have density `α : ℝ` (relative to a set `A`) if the proportion of `x ∈ S` such that `x < n` in `A` tends to `α` as `n → ∞`. When `β = ℕ` this by default defines the natural density of a set (i.e., relative to all of `ℕ`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

