-- L4DEL: intuition: The block complexity $p(n, a)$ of a sequence $a$, that is, the number of distinct blocks $a_k a_{k+1} \cdots a_{k+n-1}$ of $n$ consecutive terms of $a$. It is `⊤` when $n \ge 1$ and $a$ takes infinitely many values.
