@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Dynamics/SymbolicDynamics/BlockComplexity.lean
@decl SymbolicDynamics.blockEntropy
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: blockEntropy
-- L4DEL: intuition: The entropy of a sequence $a$, $$E(a) = \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{\log p(n, a)}{n}.$$ The limit exists because $n \mapsto \log p(n, a)$ is subadditive, so it agrees with the `limsup` used here. The value is `⊤` exactly when $a$ takes infinitely many values.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

