@decl EuclideanGeometry.IsIsoscelesTrapezoid
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsIsoscelesTrapezoid
-- L4DEL: intuition: `a b c d` are the vertices, in counter-clockwise order, of an isosceles trapezoid: they are in strictly convex position, the side `ab` is parallel to the side `cd` (the two bases), and the diagonals `ac` and `bd` have equal length. One pair of parallel sides together with equal diagonals is the classical characterization of an isosceles trapezoid; in particular it rules out non-rectangular parallelograms.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

