@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AdditionChain.lean
@decl IsAdditionChain
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsAdditionChain
-- L4DEL: intuition: An *addition chain* is a strictly increasing sequence $1 = a_0 < a_1 < \cdots < a_r$ in which every entry after the first is the sum of two (not necessarily distinct) earlier entries. `IsAdditionChain c` asserts that the list $c$ is such a chain: it starts at $1$, is strictly increasing, and every entry other than $1$ is a sum of two entries of $c$.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AdditionChain.lean
@decl IsAdditionChain.dropLast
-- L4DEL: title: Dropping the last entry of a chain leaves a chain
-- L4DEL: intuition: Dropping the last entry of a chain leaves a chain. The entries are positive, so a summand of the last entry is never the last entry itself and so survives the drop.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

