@decl Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.entrySup
-- L4DEL: title: The sup norm on the entries of a matrix: for `n = 2` this is `|(a b; c d)| = max {|a|, |b|, |c|, |d|}`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The sup norm on the entries of a matrix: for `n = 2` this is `|(a b; c d)| = max {|a|, |b|, |c|, |d|}`. The supremum is taken in `ℝ≥0` rather than `ℝ` so that it is also defined when `n` is empty, where it takes the value `0` — the right answer, since then `Matrix n n ℝ` is the zero ring.
