@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AutomorphicForm/BorelJacquet.lean
@decl Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.exists_forall_norm_le_pow_of_le
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: exists_forall_norm_le_pow_of_le
-- L4DEL: intuition: A slow-increase bound with exponent `r` gives one with any exponent `r' ≥ r`: `gnorm` is bounded below by `(Fintype.card n)⁻¹ > 0`, so enlarging the exponent costs only the constant factor `(Fintype.card n) ^ (r' - r)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AutomorphicForm/BorelJacquet.lean
@decl Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.gnorm
-- L4DEL: title: The norm `‖y‖ = max (|y|, |y⁻¹|)` on `GL n ℝ`, with `|·|` the sup norm on matrix entries
-- L4DEL: intuition: The norm `‖y‖ = max (|y|, |y⁻¹|)` on `GL n ℝ`, with `|·|` the sup norm on matrix entries. This is the norm used to define slow increase. For `G = GL n` this is exactly the archimedean factor of the norm Getz-Hahn use for a general reductive `G`: theirs is the sup of the entries of `ι y`, for `ι : G → SL (2 * n)` the embedding `y ↦ (y, (y⁻¹)ᵗ)`, whose entries are those of `y` together with those of `y⁻¹`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AutomorphicForm/BorelJacquet.lean
@decl Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.inv_card_le_gnorm
-- L4DEL: title: `gnorm` is uniformly bounded below: since `y * y⁻¹ = 1`, the entries of `y` and `y⁻¹` cannot all be small
-- L4DEL: intuition: `gnorm` is uniformly bounded below: since `y * y⁻¹ = 1`, the entries of `y` and `y⁻¹` cannot all be small. This makes the exponent in a slow-increase bound enlargeable, hence `IsSlowlyIncreasing` closed under addition.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/NumberTheory/AutomorphicForm/BorelJacquet.lean
@decl Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.IsAutomorphicForm
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsAutomorphicForm
-- L4DEL: intuition: An automorphic form for `(G, K)` in the sense of Borel-Jacquet, with `G = GL n / ℚ` and `K = O n ℝ`: `G(𝔸)` is written as `G(𝔸_f) × G(ℝ) = GL n 𝔸ᶠ[ℤ, ℚ] × GL n ℝ`, condition (a) is invariance under `ratDiagonal n`, the rational points embedded diagonally, condition (b2) is finiteness under the maximal compact `orthogonalSubgroup n`, and condition (c) is with respect to the action of the centre of the universal enveloping algebra by left invariant differential operators, `centerAction`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

