@decl IsMirimanoffPrime
-- L4DEL: title: Mirimanoff prime** A Mirimanoff prime is a prime $p$ with $3^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p^2}$, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Mirimanoff prime** A Mirimanoff prime is a prime $p$ with $3^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p^2}$, i.e. a Wieferich prime to base $3$. The name comes from Mirimanoff's 1910 result that a failure of the first case of Fermat's Last Theorem for the exponent $p$ forces this congruence.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

