@decl IsWieferichPrimeBase
-- L4DEL: title: Wieferich prime to base `a`** A prime $p$ is a Wieferich prime to base $a$ if $p^2 \mid a^{p-1} - 1$, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Wieferich prime to base `a`** A prime $p$ is a Wieferich prime to base $a$ if $p^2 \mid a^{p-1} - 1$, i.e. if $a^{p-1} \equiv 1 \pmod{p^2}$. The subtraction is truncated, so, as with `Nat.ProbablePrime`, every prime is a Wieferich prime to base $0$. For `a ≠ 0` the definition agrees with the congruence, see `isWieferichPrimeBase_iff_pow_modEq`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

