@decl FormalConjecturesForMathlib.Probability.Finset.exists_eq_zero_of_real_sum_lt_card
-- L4DEL: title: Finite probabilistic method (real form).** If `(∑ x ∈ s, (f x : ℝ)) < s.card`, then there exists `a ∈ s` with `f a = 0`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Finite probabilistic method (real form).** If `(∑ x ∈ s, (f x : ℝ)) < s.card`, then there exists `a ∈ s` with `f a = 0`. This is the same statement as `Finset.exists_eq_zero_of_sum_lt_card` after casting the counting inequality to `ℝ`; it is the convenient entry point when `f` arises as an expectation whose bound was computed in the reals (e.g. via `Real.rpow` / `Real.log`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Probability/FiniteMethod.lean
@decl FormalConjecturesForMathlib.Probability.Finset.exists_eq_zero_of_sum_lt_card
-- L4DEL: title: Finite probabilistic method (integer form).** If `∑ x ∈ s, f x < s.card`, then there exists `a ∈ s` with `f a = 0`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **Finite probabilistic method (integer form).** If `∑ x ∈ s, f x < s.card`, then there exists `a ∈ s` with `f a = 0`. **Proof idea.** Contrapositive: if every value is at least `1`, the sum is at least `s.card · 1 = s.card`, contradicting the hypothesis.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

