@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/RingTheory/CohenMacaulayModule.lean
@decl Module.IsBalancedBigCohenMacaulay
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsBalancedBigCohenMacaulay
-- L4DEL: intuition: A *balanced big Cohen-Macaulay module* over a local ring `R` is an `R`-module `M`, not necessarily finitely generated, with `m • M ≠ M` and such that every system of parameters of `R` is a regular sequence on `M`. Part of the literature calls this simply a big Cohen-Macaulay module, and reserves the weaker condition that *some* system of parameters is a regular sequence for that name. Over a Noetherian local ring the field `smul_top_ne_top` follows from `isRegular`, see `Module.smul_top_ne_top_of_isRegular`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

