@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/RingTheory/MvPolynomial/LexPlusPowers.lean
@decl MvPolynomial.hilbertFunction
-- L4DEL: title: The Hilbert function of a homogeneous ideal `I` of $k[x_1, \dots, x_n]$, sending `d` to $\dim_k I_d$
-- L4DEL: intuition: The Hilbert function of a homogeneous ideal `I` of $k[x_1, \dots, x_n]$, sending `d` to $\dim_k I_d$. This is finite, since $I_d$ is a subspace of the finite dimensional space $S_d$. Two homogeneous ideals have the same Hilbert function in this sense if and only if the graded quotients by them do, since $\dim_k (S/I)_d = \dim_k S_d - \dim_k I_d$.
