@file FormalConjecturesForMathlib/Topology/AbsoluteNeighborhoodRetract.lean
@decl IsAbsoluteNeighborhoodRetract
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: IsAbsoluteNeighborhoodRetract
-- L4DEL: intuition: A topological space `X` is an *absolute neighborhood retract* (ANR) if, whenever it is embedded as a closed subspace of a normal space `Y`, there exists a continuous retraction from some open neighborhood of `X` in `Y` onto `X`. More precisely, for every closed embedding `e : X → Y` into a normal space `Y`, there exist an open set `U ⊆ Y` containing the image of `e` and a continuous map `r : Y → X` defined on `U` such that `r ∘ e = id`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

