@file FormalConjecturesUtil/Linters/CategoryLinter.lean
@decl CategoryLinter.checkNotOpenIfSorryFree
-- L4DEL: title: Warns when a problem categorised as `research open` turns out to have a sorry-free proof
-- L4DEL: intuition: Warns when a problem categorised as `research open` turns out to have a sorry-free proof. This check used to live in the `category` attribute, at `.afterTypeChecking`, where it never fired for a theorem: proof terms elaborate asynchronously, so `value?` was still `none`. It did fire for a `def`, which is why the gap went unnoticed. `.afterCompilation` is late enough to see the proof term in an ordinary file, but not inside a module, and every file in `FormalConjecturesTest` is a module. An attribute-based check therefore cannot be given a test. A linter runs once the command has finished and works in both, so the check lives here and `findAsync?` waits on the elaboration task.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

